//@version=6
// ============================================================================
// IDX Analyzer DG2.2 [IZA]
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// VERSIONING: "DG" (Decision Gate) lineage. Every revision increments the
// number after "DG2." (DG2.0 -> DG2.1 -> DG2.2 -> ...) as a NEW file — never
// overwrite a shipped version in place, so any prior state stays reachable.
// File name and in-script shorttitle always stay in sync. DG2.0/DG2.1 stay on
// disk unchanged as revert points for this bump.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DG2.2 adds two things actually validated by NEW walk-forward research
// (`research_v24/gate2_exit_research.py`, `forecast2_research.py`,
// `forecast2_simple_model.py`; full writeup: `DG22_EDGE_RESEARCH_RESULTS.md`)
// — requested by the user as "develop Decision Gate 2.0 and its Edge, and
// upgrade to AI/TR Forecast 2.0, removing limits where warranted":
//   1. DECISION GATE 2.0 TRADE PLAN (the "Edge") — NOT a new entry signal.
//      The entry (gate2Dir==1, tier A+/A/B) is unchanged and still net-
//      negative. What was tested: can a BETTER EXIT turn the SAME entry into
//      something closer to breakeven? Answer: yes. An ATR trailing-stop (no
//      fixed R-multiple target, minimum 5-bar hold before the trail can
//      arm, maximum 30-bar hold) beat the old fixed-2R/H20 exit at every
//      trail width tested (2.0x-4.5x ATR) on BOTH the design slice (<2024)
//      and the held-out test slice (>=2024): test mean return improved from
//      -0.52% to -0.09%, test PF from 0.842 to 0.976 — still net-negative
//      (PF<1), but a large, real reduction in average loss per signal.
//      3.0x ATR was chosen over the design-best 4.5x deliberately: PF kept
//      climbing on the DESIGN slice as the trail widened (2.0x->4.5x, PF
//      0.986->1.184) but was FLAT on TEST across that same range (0.974-
//      0.976) — a classic sign the "best on design" value is overfit to the
//      design period specifically, not a real ongoing edge. 3.0x sits in the
//      middle of that flat, robust plateau. Implemented as a NEW, separate
//      hypothetical-position tracker (gate2*) — mirrors the EXISTING
//      hasPosition/trailStop mechanism structurally but is fully independent
//      of it (does not touch hasPosition, entryPrice, trailStop, or anything
//      the real owned-position logic uses).
//   2. AI FORECAST 2.0 (direction only — target/magnitude untouched, see
//      below) — the FIRST genuinely validated directional edge found in this
//      project's entire history. A proper walk-forward ML classification
//      test (train<2022, validate 2022-2023 for model selection only, test
//      >=2024 reported once) on 6 features this script already computes
//      (distance from SMA200 in ATR units, 20-bar momentum, ATR%, ADX,
//      market regime bias, RSI) beat the naive 52.50% baseline: 53.4% test
//      accuracy via a logistic-regression score portable into Pine as a
//      handful of hardcoded coefficients (a 200-tree Random Forest scored
//      higher in research, 54.2%, but cannot be hand-encoded into Pine — the
//      logistic version captures most, not all, of that edge). Compare: the
//      EXISTING kNN AI Forecast direction call scores 47.3% on the same
//      test window — BELOW its own naive baseline. This is a real but SMALL
//      edge (53.4% vs 52.5%, about 1 percentage point) — shown alongside the
//      old kNN direction call as "AI Forecast 2.0", not a replacement, so
//      both can be compared on the chart. Its price TARGET/magnitude is NOT
//      touched this round — direction only.
//   3. Chart Pattern trend-gate (`useTrendGatePattern`) default changed
//      true->false: the calibration backtest that shipped with DG2.1 found
//      it does NOT improve pattern hit-rate (slightly worse or flat on all
//      4 pattern types, DG21_CALIBRATION_AND_BACKTEST_RESULTS.md) while
//      cutting sample size ~40% — a limit that measurably wasn't helping,
//      so (per the user's own "remove limits where warranted" framing) this
//      one is actually removed. The setting remains available, just off.
//   4. `trShrink`/`aiShrink` (0.25) are DELIBERATELY NOT touched — this round
//      re-checked them and confirmed they're the opposite case from #3: a
//      previously-validated fix (research_v24, ML1.0: cuts forecast MAE
//      ~20% vs unshrunk), not an unproven limit. Removing a constraint that
//      is already known to help would make the forecast worse, not better —
//      "remove limits where warranted" cuts both ways, and this one isn't.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DG2.1 formalizes, as a proper versioned checkpoint, two fixes that were
// applied directly to the DG2.0 file after it first shipped (per explicit
// user request to fix live rather than wait for a version bump) — both are
// carried forward here unchanged, not reapplied:
//   1. LIVE-COMPILE FIX — DG2.0's first paste into TradingView Desktop threw
//      "Could not find function or function reference 'f_clamp' (CE10271)":
//      f_clamp was called by ML1.3 PRO blocks earlier in the file than its
//      old definition (inside the AI/Trend Forecast module, much further
//      down). Fixed by moving the one f_clamp definition up next to f_bold.
//      Verified by an ACTUAL TradingView Desktop compile: 0 errors, 4
//      pre-existing non-blocking style warnings (f_aiForecastUpdateHist,
//      inherited unchanged from ML1.0, out of scope here).
//   2. UI DECLUTTER FIX — user reported the panels "tidak terintegrasi
//      dengan baik" (not well integrated). Root cause, confirmed via
//      data_get_pine_labels (verbose, comparing actual price/x positions):
//      the standalone 3-line "DECISION GATE 2.0" banner label sat only ~1
//      ATR from the legacy 1-line gate label, in the same price band as the
//      candle notation tags (AK2/EXT/NO-RR/etc.) — a real collision, not
//      just a theoretical one. Fixed by deleting the standalone banner and
//      moving its content to be the FIRST content line of the existing
//      floating panel instead of a second competing label object. Confirmed
//      live: 218 label objects instead of 219, no more overlapping cluster.
//   3. MOJIBAKE FIX — user sent a screenshot of the info panel showing every
//      value after each ":" as garbled text (e.g. "SYMBOL :" itself legible,
//      the ticker/status after it unreadable). Root cause: f_bold() (used to
//      fake bold text, since Pine labels have no native bold property) maps
//      ASCII letters/digits to "Mathematical Sans-Serif Bold" Unicode code
//      points (U+1D5D4 range, outside the Basic Multilingual Plane) — these
//      do not render on this user's actual TradingView Desktop font stack,
//      while plain ASCII renders fine, which is exactly the pattern in the
//      screenshot. Fixed by removing f_bold() and its boldSrc/boldDst arrays
//      entirely (now-dead code) and using plain text everywhere it used to
//      be called: the info panel (every field), ENTRY-BUY/EXIT-SELL labels,
//      the short-term level tags (SUPPORT/RESISTANCE/TR1/TR2/STOP LOSS/
//      ENTRY-AREA), the gate label, the PATTERN ACC line, and the two
//      hand-typed "TR FORECAST"/"AI FORECAST" panel headers (same Unicode
//      block, same bug, typed directly rather than via f_bold — found by
//      grepping for the literal characters, not just the function calls).
//      This is a readability regression fix: unreadable "bold" text conveys
//      zero information, strictly worse than legible plain text.
// All three fixes are compile-verified and/or visually-verified live on
// TradingView Desktop (IDX_DLY:BBRI) — not just the structural (paren-
// balance/forward-reference) checks used for versions before DG2.0's first
// real paste.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DG2.0 (content identical to ML1.4, only identity/versioning changed) added
// "DECISION GATE 2.0" — a single synthesis of every signal this script
// computes (legacy + ML1.3 PRO), weighted by WHAT HAS ACTUALLY BEEN
// VALIDATED against idx_stocks_10y, not by how sophisticated a read looks.
// Written after an explicit professional-trader-style review of this script
// (requested by the user; full assessment given in chat, not repeated here —
// summary below is the part that changes code):
//   - dailyBullStrong/breakout (leading flags): REAL measured edge (10D
//     big-move hit rate 20.2%/18.0% vs 15.8% baseline) -> HIGH weight.
//   - Chart Pattern bias, esp. DT/DB: REAL measured edge (65.7%/70.8%
//     target-hit rate) -> HIGH weight.
//   - TR/AI Forecast DIRECTION: PROVEN to have NO edge (47-48% accuracy,
//     BELOW the 51.4% naive baseline, research_v24/results/summary.csv) ->
//     LOW weight, context only, never a primary driver.
//   - bullScorePro/bearScorePro/gradePro (ML1.3): richer context, but
//     UNVALIDATED against this dataset as of ML1.3 -> MEDIUM weight.
//   - Bandarmologi Anomali-Trap: treated as a VETO/dampener (a trap should
//     suppress conviction, not add to it), not a directional vote.
//   - buySignal itself remains what it has always been: net-negative in
//     every backtested variant to date (22-38% win rate, PF < 1 in every
//     case, research_v24/results/trading.csv + ML1.2_RESEARCH_FINDINGS.md).
//     Decision Gate 2.0 does NOT claim to fix this — it makes the same
//     honest signal legible with evidence-weighted conviction and an
//     explicit conflict flag, and scales SUGGESTED position size down when
//     conviction is low, rather than pretending a 0/1 buySignal is equally
//     trustworthy every time it fires.
// New, additive only (nothing legacy or ML1.3 is removed or reweighted):
//   - convictionScore (0-100): weighted blend of the components above.
//   - gate2Text / gate2Reason: one-line recommendation + one-line "why",
//     explicitly naming agreeing vs conflicting components.
//   - conflictFlag: true when the leading/pattern evidence and the AI/TR
//     forecast direction actively disagree — surfaced, not hidden.
//   - lotsConviction: `lots` (existing, capital/risk-based) scaled down by
//     conviction tier (A+/A full size, B 65%, C 35%, D/no-trade 0%) — a
//     standard professional risk-management practice (size DOWN on a lower-
//     quality read), not a claim about entry-timing edge.
//   - A new, visually dominant "DECISION GATE 2.0" label at the last bar —
//     the single line meant to be read first — plus a matching row in both
//     the floating panel and the detail table.
// LIVE-COMPILE FIX (2026-09-07): the first paste of this file into
// TradingView Desktop's real Pine Editor threw "Could not find function or
// function reference 'f_clamp' (CE10271)" — f_clamp was being called by
// several ML1.3/DG2.0 PRO blocks earlier in the file than its old definition
// (inside the AI/Trend Forecast module, much later down). Fixed by moving
// the ONE f_clamp definition up next to f_bold, near the top — not
// duplicated. Verified by an actual TradingView Desktop compile after the
// fix (not just the automated structural checks used for ML1.3/ML1.4/the
// first DG2.0 pass): 0 errors, 4 remaining non-blocking style warnings (all
// on the pre-existing f_aiForecastUpdateHist calls, inherited unchanged from
// ML1.0 — "should be called on each calculation for consistency", the same
// category of warning `ta.highest` used to trigger before ML1.2 moved it
// top-level; left as-is here since fixing it isn't part of this request).
// This is the first version in this session verified by a REAL compile
// rather than structural checks alone — see feedback_idx_analyzer_versioning
// memory / ML1.2's own header for why full CDP-simulated live compiles were
// previously avoided (clipboard paste via synthetic keyboard events is
// blocked; a real user-driven Cmd+A/Cmd+V, which is what happened here, is
// not).
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Full history of every prior lineage (V2.0-V2.5, ML1.0-ML1.4) that used to
// be documented in this header at length has been trimmed per explicit
// request — it remains readable in full in those files themselves (still on
// disk, both save locations) and in this project's `research_v24/` docs and
// Claude memory; nothing about the script's structure or behavior changed.
// ============================================================================

indicator("IDX Analyzer DG2.2", shorttitle = "IDXA-DG2.2", overlay = true, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 120, max_bars_back = 5000)

// ============================================================================
// REFERENCE PERIODS & INDICATORS — one place to check "how far back / how far
// forward" any module below reads, so different sections never disagree.
//   • Trend/Regime (legacy)  -> EMA10/20/50 + SMA200 stack + ADX(14), weekly
//                               gate (wBull/wBear) — unchanged, still drives
//                               buySignal/hardGates.
//   • Trend/Regime (ML1.3)   -> Auto-MTF (chart-aware HTF) + Market Index
//                               (IDX:COMPOSITE) + Sector RS — diagnostic only.
//   • Structure/S-R (legacy) -> pivotLen-bar pivots -> s1/r1 (last two
//                               confirmed pivots) — unchanged, still drives
//                               autoStop/rrOK/decision.
//   • Structure/S-R (ML1.3)  -> same pivots, clustered + EMA20-blended,
//                               tightness adaptive to timeframe/trend/ADX/
//                               velocity -> support1/resist1 ("S/R PRO"),
//                               diagnostic only.
//   • Chart Pattern Engine   -> pivLen-bar pivots (own, independent of
//                               pivotLen above), confirm within maxWait bars,
//                               track outcome for trackBars — optional
//                               prior-trend gate added in ML1.3.
//   • Volume/Akumulasi-Dist  -> legacy: per-bar candle/CLV/RVOL proxy score
//                               (accClass/distClass, drives setups/traps).
//                               ML1.3: CMF-style money-flow phase (cmfLen-bar
//                               sum) confirmed by RVOL + ROC(veloLen)
//                               velocity — diagnostic only.
//   • Bandarmologi (ML1.3)   -> Anomali-Trap and Akumulasi/Distribusi
//                               Bertahap tier both evaluated on the CURRENT
//                               bar only, confirmed against the CURRENT RVOL
//                               — never a lagging read, per definition.
//   • Skor & Grading (ML1.3) -> independent 0-100 Bull/Bear score, same-bar
//                               read across every module above — diagnostic,
//                               does not gate buySignal.
//   • AI/TR Forecast         -> unchanged from ML1.0-ML1.2: horizon-bar
//                               (default 20D) ensemble + kNN pattern-match
//                               projection, redrawn every bar from "Today".
// ============================================================================

// ---------- Inputs: Elite 20D
grpMode = "01. Mode & Position"
hasPosition = input.bool(false, "Sudah memiliki saham", group=grpMode)
avgBuy = input.float(0.0, "Harga rata-rata beli", minval=0, step=1, group=grpMode)
initialStopInput = input.float(0.0, "Stop awal manual (0 = otomatis)", minval=0, step=1, group=grpMode)
entryTime = input.time(timestamp("2025-01-01T00:00:00+07:00"), "Tanggal entry", group=grpMode)
capital = input.float(100000000, "Modal (Rp)", minval=0, step=1000000, group=grpMode)
riskPct = input.float(0.75, "Risiko per transaksi (%)", minval=0.1, maxval=2.0, step=0.05, group=grpMode)

grpFilter = "02. Filter"
minAvgValue = input.float(10000000000, "Minimum rata-rata nilai transaksi 20D (Rp)", minval=0, step=1000000000, group=grpFilter)
minRR = input.float(2.0, "Minimum risk-reward", minval=1.0, maxval=5.0, step=0.1, group=grpFilter)
maxStopPct = input.float(8.0, "Maksimum jarak stop (%)", minval=2, maxval=15, step=0.5, group=grpFilter)
maxExtensionATR = input.float(2.0, "Maksimum extension dari EMA20 (ATR)", minval=0.5, maxval=5, step=0.1, group=grpFilter)

grpLevel = "03. Struktur & Level"
pivotLen = input.int(5, "Pivot kiri/kanan", minval=2, maxval=15, group=grpLevel)
zoneATR = input.float(0.25, "Lebar setengah buy zone (ATR)", minval=0.1, maxval=1, step=0.05, group=grpLevel)
stopBufferATR = input.float(0.25, "Buffer stop (ATR)", minval=0.1, maxval=1, step=0.05, group=grpLevel)

grpFlow = "04. Akumulasi, Distribusi & Trap"
rvolSmall = input.float(1.10, "RVOL kecil", minval=1, step=0.05, group=grpFlow)
rvolMedium = input.float(1.50, "RVOL sedang", minval=1, step=0.05, group=grpFlow)
rvolLarge = input.float(2.00, "RVOL besar", minval=1, step=0.1, group=grpFlow)
rvolAnomaly = input.float(2.50, "RVOL anomali", minval=1.5, step=0.1, group=grpFlow)
trapWindow = input.int(3, "Jendela konfirmasi trap", minval=1, maxval=5, group=grpFlow)

grpVisual = "05. Tampilan"
displayMode = input.string("Standard", "Mode notasi", options=["Minimal", "Standard", "Detail"], group=grpVisual)
showMA = input.bool(true, "Tampilkan EMA/SMA", group=grpVisual)
showLevels = input.bool(true, "Tampilkan support/resistance", group=grpVisual)
showBuyZone = input.bool(false, "Tampilkan buy zone", group=grpVisual, tooltip = "Default nonaktif — area buy zone disembunyikan dari chart")
showDashboard = input.bool(true, "Tampilkan dashboard", group=grpVisual, tooltip="Master on/off untuk dashboard. Pilih bentuknya (Panel mengambang / Tabel Detail gaya V2.4 / keduanya) di input 'Mode Dashboard', grup 17 PRO — Dashboard/UI.")
showDecisionLabels = input.bool(true, "Label saat keputusan berubah", group=grpVisual)
maxDecisionLabels = input.int(80, "Maksimum label keputusan", minval=10, maxval=180, group=grpVisual)
lineTransparency = input.int(85, "Transparansi garis indikator", minval=0, maxval=95, group=grpVisual, tooltip = "Semua garis EMA/SMA/S-R/stop/target dibuat transparan pada level ini")
notationTransparency = input.int(78, "Transparansi notasi", minval=0, maxval=95, group=grpVisual, tooltip = "Transparansi latar label notasi (WAIT-S, AK2, dsb) — ukuran tetap tiny. ML1.2: default dinaikkan dari 55 ke 78 supaya benar-benar terlihat transparan (dikonfirmasi langsung di TradingView Desktop).")

// ---------- Inputs: Chart Patterns [FEELS]
grpPatCore = "06. Chart Pattern Engine"
pivLen   = input.int(3, "Swing size", minval = 3, maxval = 40, group = grpPatCore, tooltip = "Pivot width on each side. Bigger = fewer, larger patterns")
tolIn    = input.float(0.5, "Level tolerance, ATR", minval = 0.1, maxval = 2, step = 0.1, group = grpPatCore, tooltip = "How close two tops, two bottoms or two shoulders must be to count as equal")
bufIn    = input.float(0.15, "Break buffer, ATR", minval = 0, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = grpPatCore, tooltip = "Price must clear the neckline by this much to confirm the pattern")
confMode = input.string("Close", "Neckline break", options = ["Close", "Wick"], group = grpPatCore, tooltip = "Close: the bar must CLOSE beyond the neckline (strict, fewer but cleaner signals). Wick: an intrabar pierce of the neckline confirms (looser, surfaces more patterns such as inverse H&S that spike through the neckline but close back)")
voidTol  = input.float(0.0, "Extra invalidation room, ATR", minval = 0, maxval = 3, step = 0.25, group = grpPatCore, tooltip = "How far past the head/apex price may travel before a forming pattern is discarded. Higher = patterns survive deeper shakeouts (more inverse H&S and double bottoms)")
maxWait  = input.int(30, "Confirm within, bars", minval = 10, maxval = 300, group = grpPatCore, tooltip = "A forming pattern that does not break its neckline within this many bars is dropped")
trackBars = input.int(60, "Track outcome for, bars", minval = 20, maxval = 500, group = grpPatCore, tooltip = "How long to follow a confirmed pattern to see if it reached its measured target")
maxKeep  = input.int(12, "Patterns kept", minval = 1, maxval = 30, group = grpPatCore, tooltip = "Oldest confirmed patterns beyond this are removed to keep the chart clean")
tgtLen   = input.int(30, "Target line length, bars", minval = 5, maxval = 100, group = grpPatCore)
patBlockBars = input.int(5, "Blokir BUY N bar setelah pola bearish", minval = 0, maxval = 20, group = grpPatCore, tooltip = "Setelah Double Top/H&S terkonfirmasi dan belum resolved, BUY baru diblokir selama N bar ini")
patBoostBars = input.int(10, "Bonus skor N bar setelah pola bullish", minval = 0, maxval = 30, group = grpPatCore, tooltip = "Setelah Double Bottom/iH&S terkonfirmasi dan belum resolved, skor akumulasi/beli mendapat bonus selama N bar ini")

grpP = "07. Chart Pattern Types"
showDT  = input.bool(true, "Double Top",       group = grpP)
showDB  = input.bool(true, "Double Bottom",    group = grpP)
showHS  = input.bool(true, "Head & Shoulders", group = grpP)
showIHS = input.bool(true, "Inverse H&S",      group = grpP)
dblMode = input.string("Any", "Second peak / bottom", options = ["Any", "Weaker"], group = grpP, tooltip = "Weaker: only take a Double Top whose second peak is not higher than the first, and a Double Bottom whose second bottom is not lower than the first. This is the classic momentum-failure form and tends to give cleaner reversals")

grpS = "08. Chart Pattern Style"
bearCol = input.color(#f23645, "Bearish", group = grpS)
bullCol = input.color(#089981, "Bullish", group = grpS)
showTgt = input.bool(true, "Show target line", group = grpS)
showOutcome = input.bool(true, "Outcome labels", group = grpS, tooltip = "Prints a small tag where each pattern resolved. Alerts and the table work regardless")
hitTxt  = input.string("target", "Target-reached text", group = grpS, tooltip = "Label printed where a confirmed pattern reached its measured target. A check mark is prefixed automatically")
failTxt = input.string("failed", "Invalidated text", group = grpS, tooltip = "Label printed where a confirmed pattern was invalidated before reaching target. A cross is prefixed automatically")
outSizeS = input.string("Small", "Outcome text size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large"], group = grpS)
showStats = input.bool(true, "Hit-rate table", group = grpS, tooltip = "Ditampilkan sebagai baris PATTERN ACC di panel info mengambang")
minStat = input.int(1, "Min samples for table", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = grpS, tooltip = "A pattern type appears in the table once it has this many resolved samples")
txtSizeS = input.string("Small", "Text size", options = ["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large"], group = grpS)

txtSize = txtSizeS == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : txtSizeS == "Normal" ? size.normal : txtSizeS == "Large" ? size.large : size.small
resSize = outSizeS == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : outSizeS == "Normal" ? size.normal : outSizeS == "Large" ? size.large : size.small

// ---------- Inputs: IDX AI + Trend Forecast
grpFcModel = "09. Forecast Model"
horizon = input.int(20, "Horizon (hari bursa)", minval=5, maxval=60, group=grpFcModel)
regLen = input.int(20, "Panjang regresi", minval=10, maxval=100, group=grpFcModel)
wTrend = input.float(0.45, "Bobot trend", minval=0, maxval=1, step=0.05, group=grpFcModel)
wMomentum = input.float(0.20, "Bobot momentum", minval=0, maxval=1, step=0.05, group=grpFcModel)
wVolume = input.float(0.20, "Bobot volume/flow", minval=0, maxval=1, step=0.05, group=grpFcModel)
wMeanRev = input.float(0.15, "Bobot mean reversion", minval=0, maxval=1, step=0.05, group=grpFcModel)
maxForecastPct = input.float(25.0, "Batas absolut forecast (%)", minval=5, maxval=50, step=1, group=grpFcModel)

grpAiFc = "10. AI Forecast"
useaiForecast = input.bool(true, "Aktifkan AI Forecast", group=grpAiFc)
aiForecastPatternLen = input.int(20, "Panjang pola (bar)", minval=10, maxval=60, group=grpAiFc)
aiForecastDictSize = input.int(100, "Ukuran kamus pola", minval=20, maxval=100, tooltip="Jumlah pola historis yang disimpan sebagai referensi. Default 100 (naik dari 40) mengikuti kandidat D100/K5 yang tervalidasi di research_v24 — mengurangi error forecast pada backtest walk-forward. Nilai besar = konteks lebih luas tapi lebih berat dihitung pada riwayat panjang.", group=grpAiFc)
aiForecastNeighbors = input.int(5, "Jumlah tetangga terdekat", minval=1, maxval=10, tooltip="Default 5 (naik dari 3) mengikuti kandidat D100/K5 tervalidasi — lihat research_v24/results/candidate_validation.csv.", group=grpAiFc)
aiForecastWeight = input.float(0.35, "Bobot blending ke forecast utama", minval=0, maxval=1, step=0.05, tooltip="Seberapa besar hasil AI Forecast mempengaruhi drift harian gabungan", group=grpAiFc)
aiForecastWeightPower = input.float(2.0, "Pangkat inverse-distance", minval=0.5, maxval=4.0, step=0.25, tooltip="Lebih besar memberi penekanan lebih kuat pada pola yang benar-benar dekat.", group=grpAiFc)
aiForecastMinSpacing = input.int(3, "Jarak minimum antar-neighbor", minval=1, maxval=20, tooltip="Mengurangi dominasi pola historis yang hampir identik karena saling overlap.", group=grpAiFc)
aiForecastFilterLen = input.int(3, "Smoothing target AI Forecast", minval=1, maxval=20, group=grpAiFc)
aiForecastBandAtr = input.float(1.5, "Lebar band AI Forecast (ATR)", minval=0.25, maxval=5.0, step=0.25, group=grpAiFc)
showPatternShape = input.bool(true, "Tampilkan bentuk pola historis (visual)", group=grpAiFc)

grpFcRisk = "11. Forecast Validasi"
minRvol = input.float(1.0, "RVOL konfirmasi", minval=0.5, maxval=3, step=0.1, group=grpFcRisk)
minConfidence = input.float(55, "Confidence minimum (%)", minval=40, maxval=90, step=1, group=grpFcRisk)
atrInvalidation = input.float(2.0, "Invalidation (ATR)", minval=0.5, maxval=5, step=0.25, group=grpFcRisk)
showCandles = input.bool(true, "Tampilkan candle Trend Forecast", group=grpFcRisk)
showBand = input.bool(true, "Rentang ketidakpastian Trend Forecast", group=grpFcRisk)
showHistory = input.bool(true, "Simpan candle prediksi yang sudah terjadi", group=grpFcRisk)
evaluationMode = input.string("Direction + ATR tolerance", "Metode validasi", options=["Direction + ATR tolerance", "Direction only"], group=grpFcRisk)
errorToleranceATR = input.float(1.0, "Toleransi error close (ATR)", minval=0.25, maxval=3, step=0.25, group=grpFcRisk)
evaluationLookback = input.int(50, "Lookback statistik validasi", minval=20, maxval=250, group=grpFcRisk)

grpShortTerm = "12. Level Jangka Pendek (10D)"
showShortTermLevels = input.bool(true, "Tampilkan garis Support/Resistance/TR1/TR2/Stop/Entry", group=grpShortTerm)
srLookback = input.int(10, "Lookback S/R jangka pendek (bar)", minval=5, maxval=50, group=grpShortTerm, tooltip="Support/Resistance/Stop dihitung dari N bar terakhir ini; TR1 adalah titik proyeksi TR Forecast pada bar ke-N yang sama.")

grpMLCal = "13. Kalibrasi Riset (ML1.0)"
trShrink = input.float(0.25, "Shrink TR Forecast", minval=0.1, maxval=1.0, step=0.05, group=grpMLCal, tooltip="Mengalikan drift/return TR Forecast sebelum dijadikan target harga. Riset walk-forward (research_v24) menemukan 0.25 memangkas MAE ~20% dibanding forecast mentah pada data out-of-sample — ini KALIBRASI MAGNITUDO untuk model yang overconfident, BUKAN peningkatan akurasi arah (direction accuracy tidak berubah signifikan).")
aiShrink = input.float(0.25, "Shrink AI Forecast", minval=0.1, maxval=1.0, step=0.05, group=grpMLCal, tooltip="Sama seperti Shrink TR Forecast tapi untuk return AI Forecast (pencocokan pola). Default 0.25 mengikuti kandidat tervalidasi AI_D100K5_SHRINK0.25 di research_v24/results/candidate_validation.csv.")

// ---------- Inputs: ML1.3 PRO upgrades (ported from v6.2.2, diagnostic-only — see header)
grpProTrend = "14. PRO — Trend, MTF & Bandarmologi"
mtfMode = input.string("Auto", "Higher-Timeframe Mode", options=["Auto", "Manual (Weekly)"], group=grpProTrend, tooltip="Auto: HTF dipilih otomatis dari timeframe chart (Intraday->Daily, Daily->Weekly, Weekly/Monthly->Monthly) — pada chart Daily hasilnya identik dengan Manual (Weekly), yaitu gate mingguan lama (wBull/wBear) yang tidak berubah.")
useMarketRegime = input.bool(true, "Aktifkan Market Index Regime", group=grpProTrend)
marketSymbolPro = input.symbol("IDX:COMPOSITE", "Simbol Market Index", group=grpProTrend)
useSectorRS = input.bool(false, "Aktifkan Sector/Benchmark RS", group=grpProTrend, tooltip="Default OFF, sama seperti v6.2.2 — RS relatif ke benchmark sering menyesatkan tanpa benchmark sektoral yang benar-benar representatif.")
sectorSymbolPro = input.symbol("IDX:COMPOSITE", "Simbol Sector/Benchmark", group=grpProTrend, active=useSectorRS)
cmfLenPro = input.int(20, "Panjang Money Flow (CMF-style)", minval=5, group=grpProTrend)
veloLenPro = input.int(10, "Panjang Kecepatan Harga (ROC bar)", minval=3, maxval=50, group=grpProTrend)
anomalyLookbackPro = input.int(3, "Anomali: Lookback Harga (bar)", minval=1, maxval=10, group=grpProTrend)
anomalyMoveMultPro = input.float(2.0, "Anomali: Ambang Gerakan (x ATR)", minval=0.5, step=0.25, group=grpProTrend)
anomalyMaxRvolPro = input.float(0.70, "Anomali: Maks RVOL (di bawah ini dicurigai)", minval=0.1, step=0.05, group=grpProTrend)
gradualMinRvolPro = input.float(0.90, "Akum/Dist Bertahap: RVOL Minimum", minval=0.1, step=0.05, group=grpProTrend)
gradualSedangRvolPro = input.float(1.10, "Akum/Dist Bertahap: RVOL Sedang", minval=0.1, step=0.05, group=grpProTrend)
gradualBesarRvolPro = input.float(1.50, "Akum/Dist Bertahap: RVOL Besar", minval=0.1, step=0.05, group=grpProTrend)

grpProStruct = "15. PRO — Struktur, S/R & Pattern Gate"
clusterAtrPro = input.float(0.45, "Lebar Cluster S/R (ATR)", minval=0.10, step=0.05, group=grpProStruct)
adxTrendTh = input.float(20.0, "Ambang ADX Trending", minval=10, step=1, group=grpProStruct)
adxStrongTh = input.float(28.0, "Ambang ADX Strong Trend", minval=15, step=1, group=grpProStruct)
useTrendGatePattern = input.bool(false, "Chart Pattern: Wajib Trend Sebelumnya", group=grpProStruct, tooltip="Menolak Double Top/Bottom atau H&S/iH&S yang tidak didahului trend asli. DG2.2: default diubah ke OFF — backtest kalibrasi DG2.1 (91 saham) menemukan fitur ini TIDAK meningkatkan hit-rate pola (sedikit lebih rendah/setara di ke-4 pola) sambil memotong ~40% sampel. Matematika pattern matching sendiri tidak berubah.")
patternTrendLookbackPro = input.int(20, "Pattern Gate: Lookback Trend (bar)", minval=5, maxval=100, group=grpProStruct, active=useTrendGatePattern)
patternTrendGatePctPro = input.float(2.0, "Pattern Gate: Minimum Trend (%)", minval=0.0, maxval=20.0, step=0.5, group=grpProStruct, active=useTrendGatePattern) / 100

grpProScore = "16. PRO — Skor & Grading"
setupThresholdPro = input.float(60, "Setup Score", minval=40, maxval=90, step=1, group=grpProScore)
confirmThresholdPro = input.float(72, "Confirmed Score", minval=50, maxval=95, step=1, group=grpProScore)
primeThresholdPro = input.float(82, "A+ Prime Score", minval=60, maxval=100, step=1, group=grpProScore)

grpProUI = "17. PRO — Dashboard/UI"
dashboardMode = input.string("Panel", "Mode Dashboard", options=["Panel", "Tabel Detail", "Panel + Tabel"], group=grpProUI, tooltip="Panel: satu panel info mengambang (ML1.1/ML1.2). Tabel Detail: tabel 6-kolom/19-baris gaya V2.4, dibangun ulang dari variabel ML1.3 saat ini. Panel + Tabel: keduanya tampil bersamaan.")

grpGate2Plan = "18. Decision Gate 2.0 — Trade Plan (Edge)"
gate2TrailAtrMult = input.float(3.0, "Trailing Stop (x ATR)", minval=1.0, maxval=6.0, step=0.5, group=grpGate2Plan, tooltip="Divalidasi lewat riset walk-forward (research_v24/gate2_exit_research.py): mengganti target tetap 2R dengan trailing stop menurunkan rata-rata rugi per sinyal dari -0.52% ke -0.09% di data held-out (>=2024). 3.0x dipilih karena ada di tengah 'plateau' yang robust antara data desain dan data test — bukan angka 4.5x yang tampak 'terbaik' di data desain saja (tanda overfitting: makin lebar makin bagus di desain tapi DATAR di test).")
gate2MinHoldBars = input.int(5, "Minimum Tahan (bar)", minval=1, maxval=20, group=grpGate2Plan, tooltip="Trailing stop baru mulai mengetat setelah sekian bar sejak sinyal BUY BIAS muncul — mencegah stop terlalu dekat saat baru masuk.")
gate2MaxHoldBars = input.int(30, "Maksimum Tahan (bar)", minval=10, maxval=60, group=grpGate2Plan)

// ---------- BUG FIX (2026-09-08, v2.1): removed the "bold-unicode helper"
// (f_bold() + its boldSrc/boldDst substitution arrays) that used to live
// here. It substituted ASCII letters/digits with "Mathematical Sans-Serif
// Bold" Unicode code points (outside the Basic Multilingual Plane) to fake a
// bold look, since Pine labels have no native bold property. Confirmed by
// screenshot on the user's actual TradingView Desktop that these code points
// render as garbled mojibake — every f_bold()-wrapped value on the info
// panel, the ENTRY-BUY/EXIT-SELL labels, the short-term level tags, the gate
// label, and the TR/AI Forecast panel headers was unreadable, while the
// surrounding plain-ASCII text (labels, punctuation) rendered fine. Every
// call site now uses plain text instead — see the panelMsg comment further
// down for the full explanation. Now unused, so removed rather than kept as
// dead code.
// FIX (compile error CE10271 "Could not find function or function reference
// 'f_clamp'"): f_clamp is used by several ML1.3/DG2.0 PRO blocks further up
// than where it used to be defined (inside the AI/Trend Forecast module,
// much later in the file) — Pine requires a function be defined before its
// first use. Moved here, right after f_bold, so every caller (PRO blocks,
// the forecast module) reaches the SAME single definition; the old spot
// down in the forecast module had its definition removed, not duplicated.
f_clamp(_x, _lo, _hi) => math.max(_lo, math.min(_hi, _x))


// ---------- Shared base calculations (computed once per bar, used by every module below)
ema10 = ta.ema(close, 10)
ema20 = ta.ema(close, 20)
ema50 = ta.ema(close, 50)
sma200 = ta.sma(close, 200)
rsi14 = ta.rsi(close, 14)
[macdLine, macdSignal, macdHist] = ta.macd(close, 12, 26, 9)
[diPlus, diMinus, adx14] = ta.dmi(14, 14)
atr14 = ta.atr(14)
volMA20 = ta.sma(volume, 20)
rvol = volMA20 > 0 ? volume / volMA20 : 0.0
avgValue20 = ta.sma(close * volume, 20)

rng = math.max(high - low, syminfo.mintick)
body = math.abs(close - open)
bodyRatio = body / rng
upperWick = high - math.max(open, close)
lowerWick = math.min(open, close) - low
clv = (close - low) / rng
closeUpper60 = clv >= 0.60

// One confirmed Weekly call, shared by the Elite decision engine (wBull/wBear/
// wState) and the Forecast module (wRegime, derived below — not recomputed).
[wClose, wEma20, wEma20Prev, wRsi] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W", [close[1], ta.ema(close, 20)[1], ta.ema(close, 20)[2], ta.rsi(close, 14)[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
wBull = wClose > wEma20 and wEma20 > wEma20Prev and wRsi > 50
wBear = wClose < wEma20 and wEma20 < wEma20Prev and wRsi < 45
wState = wBull ? "BULL" : wBear ? "BEAR" : "NEUTRAL"

// ---------- ML1.3: Auto-MTF, Market Index & Sector RS (diagnostic — parallel to
// wBull/wBear above, which keeps gating buySignal/hardGates unchanged). On a
// Daily chart, mtfTF resolves to "W" — identical target to the weekly call
// above — so this ADDS a genuinely different read (its own EMA20/EMA50 stack
// test, not a rsi/ema-slope test) rather than duplicating it.
// BUG FIX (2026-09-08, v2.1 — Pine v6 standards pass): this call used to
// request UNSHIFTED close/ema20/ema50 combined with lookahead=
// barmerge.lookahead_on — that specific combination is a documented Pine
// repainting/lookahead bug (lookahead_on without a [1] offset lets an
// in-progress higher-timeframe bar's still-forming values leak backward onto
// earlier lower-timeframe bars within the same HTF period, e.g. Monday could
// see where that week ends up closing). The wBull/wBear call above already
// avoids this correctly by shifting every field by [1] (always reading the
// last CLOSED higher-timeframe bar); this call now does the same.
autoHTF = timeframe.isintraday ? "D" : timeframe.isdaily ? "W" : "M"
mtfTF = mtfMode == "Auto" ? autoHTF : "W"
[htfClose, htfEma20, htfEma50] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, mtfTF, [close[1], ta.ema(close, 20)[1], ta.ema(close, 50)[1]], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
mtfBias = htfClose > htfEma20 and htfEma20 > htfEma50 ? 1 : htfClose < htfEma20 and htfEma20 < htfEma50 ? -1 : 0
mtfText = mtfBias == 1 ? "BULL" : mtfBias == -1 ? "BEAR" : "NEUTRAL"
// BUG FIX (2026-09-08, v2.1 — "double pull data" audit): both calls below
// used to run UNCONDITIONALLY every bar even when their own toggle
// (useMarketRegime / useSectorRS) was off — useSectorRS defaults to false,
// so every user was pulling and discarding sector data by default. Both are
// now gated behind their toggle (the documented Pine idiom for optional
// request.security() calls — the compiler skips the pull entirely when a
// "simple" input-derived condition is false, not just the downstream math).
// Sector is further deduplicated against Market: when both are enabled AND
// point at the same symbol (the shared "IDX:COMPOSITE" default), the sector
// benchmark reuses the market close already fetched instead of issuing a
// second identical request.security() call for the same (symbol,timeframe).
float mCloseP = na
float mEma20P = na
float mEma50P = na
if useMarketRegime
    [mc, me20, me50] = request.security(marketSymbolPro, timeframe.period, [close, ta.ema(close, 20), ta.ema(close, 50)], ignore_invalid_symbol=true)
    mCloseP := mc
    mEma20P := me20
    mEma50P := me50
marketBias = not useMarketRegime or na(mCloseP) ? 0 : mCloseP > mEma20P and mEma20P > mEma50P ? 1 : mCloseP < mEma20P and mEma20P < mEma50P ? -1 : 0
marketText = not useMarketRegime ? "OFF" : marketBias == 1 ? "BULL" : marketBias == -1 ? "BEAR" : "NEUTRAL"
float benchClosePro = na
if useSectorRS
    if useMarketRegime and sectorSymbolPro == marketSymbolPro
        benchClosePro := mCloseP
    else
        benchClosePro := request.security(sectorSymbolPro, timeframe.period, close, ignore_invalid_symbol=true)
rsRatioPro = useSectorRS and not na(benchClosePro) and benchClosePro != 0 ? close / benchClosePro : na
rsMAPro = ta.ema(rsRatioPro, 20)
rsBias = not useSectorRS or na(rsRatioPro) ? 0 : rsRatioPro > rsMAPro and rsMAPro > rsMAPro[5] ? 1 : rsRatioPro < rsMAPro and rsMAPro < rsMAPro[5] ? -1 : 0
rsText = not useSectorRS ? "OFF" : rsBias == 1 ? "STRONG" : rsBias == -1 ? "WEAK" : "NEUTRAL"

// ============================================================================
// DG2.2: AI FORECAST 2.0 — direction-only logistic-regression score. The
// FIRST genuinely validated directional edge found in this project's history
// (test accuracy 53.4% vs the 52.50% naive baseline, walk-forward: trained
// <2022, model chosen on 2022-2023 validation only, tested >=2024 once — see
// DG22_EDGE_RESEARCH_RESULTS.md). A 200-tree Random Forest scored higher in
// research (54.2%) but can't be hand-encoded into Pine; this logistic
// version captures most, not all, of that edge — shown as a genuinely small
// (~1pp) but real edge, not a strong one. Coefficients/scaler stats below
// are frozen from that research run (research_v24/forecast2_simple_model.py)
// — they are NOT re-fit live in Pine (this is a fixed linear score, exactly
// like a coefficients-only deployment of a trained model, standard practice
// once a model is frozen). Direction ONLY — the price TARGET/magnitude this
// script forecasts elsewhere (TR/AI Forecast below) is untouched by this.
// Reuses close/sma200/atr14/adx14/rsi14 (base calcs above) and marketBias
// (just computed above, from REAL IDX:COMPOSITE data when available — better
// than the equal-weighted proxy the offline research had to use) — no new
// data pulled, no recomputation of anything that already exists.
af2_distSma200Atr = atr14 > 0 ? (close - sma200) / atr14 : 0.0
af2_mom20 = close[20] != 0 ? close / close[20] - 1 : 0.0
af2_atrPct = close != 0 ? atr14 / close * 100 : 0.0
af2_z1 = (af2_distSma200Atr - (-4.207273)) / 311.415115
af2_z2 = (af2_mom20 - 0.015898) / 0.179317
af2_z3 = (af2_atrPct - 3.794796) / 2.106997
af2_z4 = (adx14 - 26.184254) / 12.210904
af2_z5 = (marketBias - 0.171254) / 0.806202
af2_z6 = (rsi14 - 49.934481) / 12.955396
af2_score = -0.045571 + (-1.094955 * af2_z1) + (-0.042770 * af2_z2) + (0.097402 * af2_z3) + (0.086939 * af2_z4) + (-0.066760 * af2_z5) + (0.027976 * af2_z6)
af2_prob = 1.0 / (1.0 + math.exp(-af2_score))
af2Direction = af2_prob > 0.5 ? "UP" : "DOWN"
af2ConfidencePct = math.abs(af2_prob - 0.5) * 200  // 0% at prob=0.5 (coin flip) up to 100% at prob=0 or 1

// ---------- V2.1: candlestick pattern recognition (feeds acc/dist scores below)
bodyPrev = math.abs(close[1] - open[1])
body2 = math.abs(close[2] - open[2])
isBullEngulf = close > open and close[1] < open[1] and close >= open[1] and open <= close[1] and body > bodyPrev
isBearEngulf = close < open and close[1] > open[1] and close <= open[1] and open >= close[1] and body > bodyPrev
isHammer = lowerWick >= body * 2 and upperWick <= body * 0.5 and bodyRatio <= 0.4
isShootingStar = upperWick >= body * 2 and lowerWick <= body * 0.5 and bodyRatio <= 0.4
isDoji = bodyRatio <= 0.08
smallMid = math.abs(close[1] - open[1]) <= body2 * 0.35
isMorningStar = close[2] < open[2] and body2 > 0 and smallMid and close > open and close > (open[2] + close[2]) / 2
isEveningStar = close[2] > open[2] and body2 > 0 and smallMid and close < open and close < (open[2] + close[2]) / 2
isPiercing = close[1] < open[1] and close > open and open < close[1] and close > (open[1] + close[1]) / 2 and close < open[1]
isDarkCloud = close[1] > open[1] and close < open and open > close[1] and close < (open[1] + close[1]) / 2 and close > open[1]

candleBullScore = (isMorningStar ? 2 : 0) + (isBullEngulf ? 2 : 0) + (isPiercing ? 1 : 0) + (isHammer ? 1 : 0)
candleBearScore = (isEveningStar ? 2 : 0) + (isBearEngulf ? 2 : 0) + (isDarkCloud ? 1 : 0) + (isShootingStar ? 1 : 0)
candleName = isMorningStar ? "Morning Star" : isBullEngulf ? "Bull Engulf" : isPiercing ? "Piercing" : isHammer ? "Hammer" : isEveningStar ? "Evening Star" : isBearEngulf ? "Bear Engulf" : isDarkCloud ? "Dark Cloud" : isShootingStar ? "Shooting Star" : isDoji ? "Doji" : "-"

// ---------- Chart Patterns: state (kept ahead of Elite scoring so its bias can feed it)
type Pat
    int   kind
    int   dir
    float neck
    float neckSlope
    int   neckX
    float apex
    int   apexBar
    float target
    float invalid
    float ext
    int   confBar
    int   bornBar
    int   coreS
    int   trailB
    bool  confirmed
    int   result
    array<int>   px
    array<float> py
    array<line>  segs
    line  neckLn
    line  tgtLn
    box   zone
    label tag
    label resTag

var pats  = array.new<Pat>()
var zzB = array.new<int>()
var zzP = array.new<float>()
var zzD = array.new<int>()
var zzT = array.new<float>()  // ML1.3: trend% at each pivot's push time, for the optional trend-gate below
var hits = array.new<int>(4, 0)
var res  = array.new<int>(4, 0)

// Shares atr14 from the shared base-calculations block instead of recomputing.
tol = atr14 * tolIn
buf = atr14 * bufIn

cpPh = ta.pivothigh(pivLen, pivLen)
cpPl = ta.pivotlow(pivLen, pivLen)

f_name(int k) =>
    k == 1 ? "Double Top" : k == 2 ? "Double Bottom" : k == 3 ? "Head & Shoulders" : "Inverse Head & Shoulders"

f_enabled(int k) =>
    k == 1 ? showDT : k == 2 ? showDB : k == 3 ? showHS : showIHS

f_neckAt(Pat p, int b) =>
    p.neck + p.neckSlope * (b - p.neckX)

//--- ML1.3: trend% behind a pivot at `back` bars ago, over patternTrendLookbackPro
// bars before it — pushed into zzT at the same time as the pivot itself, so
// the trend-gate check later never needs to recompute or re-walk history.
f_pivotTrendPro(int back) =>
    refC = close[back + patternTrendLookbackPro]
    pivC = close[back]
    refC != 0 ? (pivC - refC) / refC : 0.0

//--- zigzag push, returns true only when a genuinely new pivot is appended
f_zzPush(int b, float pr, int d, float trendPct) =>
    n = array.size(zzD)
    appended = false
    if n == 0
        array.push(zzB, b)
        array.push(zzP, pr)
        array.push(zzD, d)
        array.push(zzT, trendPct)
        appended := true
    else
        li = n - 1
        if array.get(zzD, li) == d
            lp = array.get(zzP, li)
            if (d == 1 and pr > lp) or (d == -1 and pr < lp)
                array.set(zzP, li, pr)
                array.set(zzB, li, b)
                array.set(zzT, li, trendPct)
        else
            array.push(zzB, b)
            array.push(zzP, pr)
            array.push(zzD, d)
            array.push(zzT, trendPct)
            appended := true
    while array.size(zzD) > 20
        array.shift(zzB)
        array.shift(zzP)
        array.shift(zzD)
        array.shift(zzT)
    appended

f_newPat(int kind, int dir, float neck, float neckSlope, int neckX, float apex, int apexBar, float invalid, float ext) =>
    p = Pat.new()
    p.kind := kind
    p.dir := dir
    p.neck := neck
    p.neckSlope := neckSlope
    p.neckX := neckX
    p.apex := apex
    p.apexBar := apexBar
    p.invalid := invalid
    p.ext := ext
    p.bornBar := bar_index
    p.confirmed := false
    p.result := 0
    p.px := array.new<int>()
    p.py := array.new<float>()
    p.segs := array.new<line>()
    array.push(pats, p)
    p

f_addPt(Pat p, int b, float v) =>
    array.push(p.px, b)
    array.push(p.py, v)

//--- one pattern per region: reject a new span that overlaps an existing one
f_regionTaken(int s, int e) =>
    taken = false
    sp = e - s
    i = 0
    while i < array.size(pats) and not taken
        p = array.get(pats, i)
        m = array.size(p.px)
        if m >= 2
            ps = array.get(p.px, 0)
            pe = array.get(p.px, m - 1)
            ov = math.min(e, pe) - math.max(s, ps)
            if ov > 0.15 * math.min(sp, pe - ps)
                taken := true
        i += 1
    taken

//--- bar where price actually crosses the neckline level, walking back from the first peak
f_crossBar(int fromBar, int toBar, float level, bool bear, int maxBack, float slp) =>
    cb = -1
    done = false
    lim = math.max(1, math.min(maxBack, fromBar - toBar))
    for k = 1 to lim
        o = bar_index - fromBar + k
        lv = level - slp * k
        if not done and o >= 0 and o <= 4990 and ((bear and low[o] <= lv) or ((not bear) and high[o] >= lv))
            cb := fromBar - k
            done := true
    cb

//--- match the newest pivots against templates (dirs alternate by construction)
f_matchHigh() =>
    n = array.size(zzD)
    matched5 = false
    if n >= 5 and showHS
        ls = array.get(zzP, n - 5)
        t1 = array.get(zzP, n - 4)
        hd = array.get(zzP, n - 3)
        t2 = array.get(zzP, n - 2)
        rs = array.get(zzP, n - 1)
        lsBar = array.get(zzB, n - 5)
        lsTrendPro = array.get(zzT, n - 5)
        legW = math.max(3, int((array.get(zzB, n - 1) - lsBar) / 4))
        b1 = array.get(zzB, n - 4)
        b2 = array.get(zzB, n - 2)
        slope = (t2 - t1) / (b2 - b1)
        crossB = f_crossBar(lsBar, array.get(zzB, math.max(0, n - 6)), t1 + slope * (lsBar - b1), true, 2 * legW, slope)
        startB = crossB >= 0 ? crossB : (n >= 6 ? array.get(zzB, n - 6) : lsBar)
        trailBar = array.get(zzB, n - 1) + legW
        trendOkHS = not useTrendGatePattern or lsTrendPro >= patternTrendGatePctPro
        if hd > ls + tol and hd > rs + tol and math.abs(ls - rs) <= 2 * tol and math.abs(t1 - t2) <= 0.35 * (hd - math.min(t1, t2)) and trendOkHS and not f_regionTaken(startB, trailBar)
            p = f_newPat(3, -1, t1, slope, b1, hd, array.get(zzB, n - 3), rs, hd)
            p.coreS := startB
            p.trailB := trailBar
            if crossB >= 0
                f_addPt(p, crossB, t1 + slope * (crossB - b1))
            else if n >= 6
                f_addPt(p, array.get(zzB, n - 6), array.get(zzP, n - 6))
            f_addPt(p, lsBar, ls)
            f_addPt(p, b1, t1)
            f_addPt(p, array.get(zzB, n - 3), hd)
            f_addPt(p, b2, t2)
            f_addPt(p, array.get(zzB, n - 1), rs)
            matched5 := true
    if n >= 3 and showDT and not matched5
        h1 = array.get(zzP, n - 3)
        l1 = array.get(zzP, n - 2)
        h2 = array.get(zzP, n - 1)
        h1Bar = array.get(zzB, n - 3)
        h1TrendPro = array.get(zzT, n - 3)
        legW = math.max(3, int((array.get(zzB, n - 1) - h1Bar) / 2))
        crossB = f_crossBar(h1Bar, array.get(zzB, math.max(0, n - 4)), l1, true, 2 * legW, 0.0)
        startB = crossB >= 0 ? crossB : (n >= 4 ? array.get(zzB, n - 4) : h1Bar)
        trailBar = array.get(zzB, n - 1) + legW
        trendOkDT = not useTrendGatePattern or h1TrendPro >= patternTrendGatePctPro
        if math.abs(h1 - h2) <= tol and (dblMode == "Any" or h2 <= h1 + tol * 0.25) and math.min(h1, h2) - l1 > 1.5 * tol and trendOkDT and not f_regionTaken(startB, trailBar)
            ex = math.max(h1, h2)
            p = f_newPat(1, -1, l1, 0.0, array.get(zzB, n - 2), (h1 + h2) / 2, array.get(zzB, n - 1), ex, ex)
            p.coreS := startB
            p.trailB := trailBar
            if crossB >= 0
                f_addPt(p, crossB, l1)
            else if n >= 4
                f_addPt(p, array.get(zzB, n - 4), array.get(zzP, n - 4))
            f_addPt(p, h1Bar, h1)
            f_addPt(p, array.get(zzB, n - 2), l1)
            f_addPt(p, array.get(zzB, n - 1), h2)

f_matchLow() =>
    n = array.size(zzD)
    matched5 = false
    if n >= 5 and showIHS
        ls = array.get(zzP, n - 5)
        t1 = array.get(zzP, n - 4)
        hd = array.get(zzP, n - 3)
        t2 = array.get(zzP, n - 2)
        rs = array.get(zzP, n - 1)
        lsBar = array.get(zzB, n - 5)
        lsTrendPro = array.get(zzT, n - 5)
        legW = math.max(3, int((array.get(zzB, n - 1) - lsBar) / 4))
        b1 = array.get(zzB, n - 4)
        b2 = array.get(zzB, n - 2)
        slope = (t2 - t1) / (b2 - b1)
        crossB = f_crossBar(lsBar, array.get(zzB, math.max(0, n - 6)), t1 + slope * (lsBar - b1), false, 2 * legW, slope)
        startB = crossB >= 0 ? crossB : (n >= 6 ? array.get(zzB, n - 6) : lsBar)
        trailBar = array.get(zzB, n - 1) + legW
        trendOkIHS = not useTrendGatePattern or lsTrendPro <= -patternTrendGatePctPro
        if hd < ls - tol and hd < rs - tol and math.abs(ls - rs) <= 2 * tol and math.abs(t1 - t2) <= 0.35 * (math.max(t1, t2) - hd) and trendOkIHS and not f_regionTaken(startB, trailBar)
            p = f_newPat(4, 1, t1, slope, b1, hd, array.get(zzB, n - 3), rs, hd)
            p.coreS := startB
            p.trailB := trailBar
            if crossB >= 0
                f_addPt(p, crossB, t1 + slope * (crossB - b1))
            else if n >= 6
                f_addPt(p, array.get(zzB, n - 6), array.get(zzP, n - 6))
            f_addPt(p, lsBar, ls)
            f_addPt(p, b1, t1)
            f_addPt(p, array.get(zzB, n - 3), hd)
            f_addPt(p, b2, t2)
            f_addPt(p, array.get(zzB, n - 1), rs)
            matched5 := true
    if n >= 3 and showDB and not matched5
        l1 = array.get(zzP, n - 3)
        h1 = array.get(zzP, n - 2)
        l2 = array.get(zzP, n - 1)
        l1Bar = array.get(zzB, n - 3)
        l1TrendPro = array.get(zzT, n - 3)
        legW = math.max(3, int((array.get(zzB, n - 1) - l1Bar) / 2))
        crossB = f_crossBar(l1Bar, array.get(zzB, math.max(0, n - 4)), h1, false, 2 * legW, 0.0)
        startB = crossB >= 0 ? crossB : (n >= 4 ? array.get(zzB, n - 4) : l1Bar)
        trailBar = array.get(zzB, n - 1) + legW
        trendOkDB = not useTrendGatePattern or l1TrendPro <= -patternTrendGatePctPro
        if math.abs(l1 - l2) <= tol and (dblMode == "Any" or l2 >= l1 - tol * 0.25) and h1 - math.max(l1, l2) > 1.5 * tol and trendOkDB and not f_regionTaken(startB, trailBar)
            ex = math.min(l1, l2)
            p = f_newPat(2, 1, h1, 0.0, array.get(zzB, n - 2), (l1 + l2) / 2, array.get(zzB, n - 1), ex, ex)
            p.coreS := startB
            p.trailB := trailBar
            if crossB >= 0
                f_addPt(p, crossB, h1)
            else if n >= 4
                f_addPt(p, array.get(zzB, n - 4), array.get(zzP, n - 4))
            f_addPt(p, l1Bar, l1)
            f_addPt(p, array.get(zzB, n - 2), h1)
            f_addPt(p, array.get(zzB, n - 1), l2)

//--- first bar after the last pivot where a candle actually crosses the neckline
f_crossFwd(Pat p) =>
    mm = array.size(p.px)
    lastB = array.get(p.px, mm - 1)
    tb = p.confBar
    done = false
    lim = math.max(1, p.confBar - lastB)
    for k = 1 to lim
        b = lastB + k
        o = bar_index - b
        lv = f_neckAt(p, b)
        if not done and o >= 0 and ((p.dir == -1 and low[o] <= lv) or (p.dir == 1 and high[o] >= lv))
            tb := b
            done := true
    tb

f_draw(Pat p) =>
    col = p.dir == -1 ? bearCol : bullCol
    tb = f_crossFwd(p)
    f_addPt(p, tb, f_neckAt(p, tb))
    p.trailB := math.max(p.trailB, tb)
    m = array.size(p.px)
    pmin = array.get(p.py, 0)
    pmax = pmin
    for k = 0 to m - 1
        v = array.get(p.py, k)
        pmin := math.min(pmin, v)
        pmax := math.max(pmax, v)
    if m >= 2
        for k = 0 to m - 2
            ln = line.new(array.get(p.px, k), array.get(p.py, k), array.get(p.px, k + 1), array.get(p.py, k + 1), color = col, width = 3)
            array.push(p.segs, ln)
    p.neckLn := line.new(p.coreS, f_neckAt(p, p.coreS), p.trailB, f_neckAt(p, p.trailB), color = col, style = line.style_dashed, width = 2)
    if showTgt
        p.tgtLn := line.new(p.confBar, p.target, p.confBar + tgtLen, p.target, color = color.new(col, 40), style = line.style_dotted, width = 1)
    tagY = p.dir == -1 ? pmax : pmin
    p.tag := label.new(p.apexBar, tagY, f_name(p.kind), style = p.dir == -1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color = color.new(col, 15), textcolor = color.new(color.black, 10), size = txtSize)

f_delete(Pat p) =>
    if array.size(p.segs) > 0
        for k = 0 to array.size(p.segs) - 1
            line.delete(array.get(p.segs, k))
    line.delete(p.neckLn)
    line.delete(p.tgtLn)
    box.delete(p.zone)
    label.delete(p.tag)
    label.delete(p.resTag)

// ---------- Chart Patterns: engine, state mutates on closed bars only
bearConf = false
bullConf = false
tgtHit   = false
patFail  = false

if barstate.isconfirmed
    if not na(cpPh)
        if f_zzPush(bar_index - pivLen, cpPh, 1, f_pivotTrendPro(pivLen))
            f_matchHigh()
    if not na(cpPl)
        if f_zzPush(bar_index - pivLen, cpPl, -1, f_pivotTrendPro(pivLen))
            f_matchLow()

    i = 0
    while i < array.size(pats)
        p = array.get(pats, i)
        gone = false
        if not p.confirmed
            neckNow = f_neckAt(p, bar_index)
            vtol = tol + atr14 * voidTol
            if p.dir == -1
                if high > p.ext + vtol
                    gone := true
                else if (confMode == "Wick" ? low : close) < neckNow - buf
                    p.confirmed := true
            else
                if low < p.ext - vtol
                    gone := true
                else if (confMode == "Wick" ? high : close) > neckNow + buf
                    p.confirmed := true
            if not gone and not p.confirmed and bar_index - p.bornBar > maxWait
                gone := true
            if p.confirmed
                p.confBar := bar_index
                neckC = f_neckAt(p, bar_index)
                height = p.dir == -1 ? p.apex - f_neckAt(p, p.apexBar) : f_neckAt(p, p.apexBar) - p.apex
                p.target := p.dir == -1 ? neckC - height : neckC + height
                f_draw(p)
                if p.dir == -1
                    bearConf := true
                else
                    bullConf := true
        else if p.result == 0
            if p.dir == -1
                if low <= p.target
                    p.result := 1
                else if close >= p.invalid
                    p.result := 2
            else
                if high >= p.target
                    p.result := 1
                else if close <= p.invalid
                    p.result := 2
            if p.result == 0 and bar_index - p.confBar > trackBars
                p.result := 3
            if p.result == 1 or p.result == 2 or p.result == 3
                ki = p.kind - 1
                array.set(res, ki, array.get(res, ki) + 1)
                if p.result == 1
                    array.set(hits, ki, array.get(hits, ki) + 1)
                    col = p.dir == -1 ? bearCol : bullCol
                    if showTgt and not na(p.tgtLn)
                        line.set_x2(p.tgtLn, bar_index)
                    if showOutcome
                        p.resTag := label.new(bar_index, p.target, "✓ " + hitTxt, style = p.dir == -1 ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color = color.new(col, 100), textcolor = color.new(color.black, 10), size = resSize)
                    tgtHit := true
                else if p.result == 2
                    if showOutcome
                        p.resTag := label.new(bar_index, p.invalid, "✕ " + failTxt, style = p.dir == -1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color = color.new(color.gray, 100), textcolor = color.new(color.black, 10), size = resSize)
                    patFail := true
        if gone
            f_delete(p)
            array.remove(pats, i)
        else
            i += 1

    //--- cap confirmed patterns, oldest first
    cnt = 0
    if array.size(pats) > 0
        for k = 0 to array.size(pats) - 1
            if array.get(pats, k).confirmed
                cnt += 1
    while cnt > maxKeep
        idx = -1
        j = 0
        while j < array.size(pats) and idx < 0
            if array.get(pats, j).confirmed
                idx := j
            j += 1
        if idx >= 0
            f_delete(array.get(pats, idx))
            array.remove(pats, idx)
        cnt -= 1

// ---------- Cross-wire the Chart Pattern engine's bias into Elite scoring below.
// Finds the most-recently-confirmed, still-unresolved pattern and its age in bars.
patBiasDir = 0
patBiasAge = 999999
if array.size(pats) > 0
    for k = 0 to array.size(pats) - 1
        pp = array.get(pats, k)
        if pp.confirmed and pp.result == 0
            age = bar_index - pp.confBar
            if age < patBiasAge
                patBiasAge := age
                patBiasDir := pp.dir
patternBearBlock = patBiasDir == -1 and patBiasAge <= patBlockBars
patternBullBoost = patBiasDir == 1 and patBiasAge <= patBoostBars

// ---------- Elite 20D: confirmed market structure (bar indices tracked for reference lines)
ph = ta.pivothigh(high, pivotLen, pivotLen)
pl = ta.pivotlow(low, pivotLen, pivotLen)
var float lastPH = na
var int   lastPHBar = na
var float prevPH = na
var int   prevPHBar = na
var float lastPL = na
var int   lastPLBar = na
var float prevPL = na
var int   prevPLBar = na
if not na(ph)
    prevPH := lastPH
    prevPHBar := lastPHBar
    lastPH := ph
    lastPHBar := bar_index - pivotLen
if not na(pl)
    prevPL := lastPL
    prevPLBar := lastPLBar
    lastPL := pl
    lastPLBar := bar_index - pivotLen

hh = not na(lastPH) and not na(prevPH) and lastPH > prevPH
hl = not na(lastPL) and not na(prevPL) and lastPL > prevPL
lh = not na(lastPH) and not na(prevPH) and lastPH < prevPH
ll = not na(lastPL) and not na(prevPL) and lastPL < prevPL
bosBull = not na(lastPH) and close > lastPH and close[1] <= lastPH
bosBear = not na(lastPL) and close < lastPL and close[1] >= lastPL
structureBull = (hh and hl) or (hl and close > ema20)
structureBear = (lh and ll) or bosBear
structureText = bosBull ? "BOS+" : bosBear ? "BOS-" : structureBull ? "HH-HL" : structureBear ? "LH-LL" : "MIXED"

// Last two confirmed pivots are stable and lightweight chart levels.
s1 = lastPL
s2 = prevPL
r1 = lastPH
r2 = prevPH

// ---------- Elite 20D: trend regime (ADX confirmation added to BULL STRONG)
ema20Up = ema20 > ema20[1]
ema50Up = ema50 > ema50[1]
dailyBullStrong = close > ema20 and ema20 > ema50 and ema20Up and ema50Up and close > sma200 and rsi14 > 50 and adx14 > 20
dailyBullEarly = close > ema20 and ema20Up and (bosBull or hl)
dailyBear = close < ema20 and ema20 < ema50 and not ema20Up and rsi14 < 45
dailySideways = adx14 < 20 and math.abs(ema20 - ema50) <= atr14 * 0.5
trendState = dailyBullStrong ? "BULL STRONG" : dailyBullEarly ? "BULL EARLY" : dailyBear ? "BEAR" : dailySideways ? "SIDEWAYS" : "NEUTRAL"

// ---------- ML1.3: price velocity (ROC), shared by S/R PRO tightness below
// AND the Bandarmologi block further down — computed once here, not twice.
velocityPro = ta.roc(close, veloLenPro)
veloHotPro = math.abs(velocityPro) >= (atr14 / close * 100) * 1.5

// ---------- ML1.3: adaptive tightness + clustered/MA-blended "S/R PRO"
// (support1/resist1), diagnostic — s1/r1 above keep driving autoStop/rrOK/
// decision unchanged. Reuses lastPH/prevPH/lastPL/prevPL (already tracked
// above) — no second pivot pass. tfTightness is a continuous log-scale base
// by timeframe seconds, tightened when the trend is convicted/ADX is strong/
// price velocity is hot, widened otherwise — same mechanism v6.2.2 validated.
tfSecondsPro = timeframe.in_seconds()
tfBaseTightnessPro = tfSecondsPro > 0 ? f_clamp(-0.460 + 0.1172 * math.log(tfSecondsPro), 0.40, 1.45) : 0.85
trendConvictionFactorPro = dailyBullStrong or dailyBear ? 0.82 : dailyBullEarly ? 0.95 : 1.15
adxRegimeFactorPro = adx14 >= adxStrongTh ? 0.90 : adx14 <= adxTrendTh * 0.6 ? 1.10 : 1.0
veloAdaptFactorPro = veloHotPro ? 0.90 : 1.0
tfTightnessPro = f_clamp(tfBaseTightnessPro * trendConvictionFactorPro * adxRegimeFactorPro * veloAdaptFactorPro, 0.35, 1.25)
effClusterAtrPro = clusterAtrPro * tfTightnessPro
supportClusteredPro = not na(lastPL) and not na(prevPL) and math.abs(lastPL - prevPL) <= atr14 * effClusterAtrPro ? (lastPL + prevPL) / 2.0 : s1
resistClusteredPro = not na(lastPH) and not na(prevPH) and math.abs(lastPH - prevPH) <= atr14 * effClusterAtrPro ? (lastPH + prevPH) / 2.0 : r1
maSupportCandidatePro = (structureBull or dailyBullStrong or dailyBullEarly) and ema20 < close ? ema20 : na
maResistCandidatePro = (structureBear or dailyBear) and ema20 > close ? ema20 : na
support1 = not na(maSupportCandidatePro) and not na(supportClusteredPro) and maSupportCandidatePro > supportClusteredPro ? maSupportCandidatePro : supportClusteredPro
resist1 = not na(maResistCandidatePro) and not na(resistClusteredPro) and maResistCandidatePro < resistClusteredPro ? maResistCandidatePro : resistClusteredPro

// ---------- Elite 20D: location, zones and liquidity
liquid = avgValue20 >= minAvgValue and volMA20 > 0 and atr14 > 0
nearSupport = not na(s1) and math.abs(close - s1) <= atr14 * 0.75
nearResistance = not na(r1) and math.abs(close - r1) <= atr14 * 0.75
emaConfluence = not na(s1) and math.abs(s1 - ema20) <= atr14 * 0.5
zoneCenter = emaConfluence ? (s1 + ema20) / 2 : not na(s1) ? s1 : ema20
buyZoneLow = zoneCenter - zoneATR * atr14
buyZoneHigh = zoneCenter + zoneATR * atr14
inBuyZone = low <= buyZoneHigh and high >= buyZoneLow
extensionATR = atr14 > 0 ? (close - ema20) / atr14 : 0.0
overextended = extensionATR > maxExtensionATR or (close > ema20 and (close - ema20) / ema20 * 100 > 10)

// ---------- Elite 20D: price-volume accumulation/distribution proxy scores
// Candlestick pattern score and Chart Pattern bias feed in directly.
int accScore = 0
accScore += clv >= 0.55 ? 1 : 0
accScore += clv >= 0.70 ? 1 : 0
accScore += rvol >= 1.20 ? 1 : 0
accScore += rvol >= rvolMedium ? 1 : 0
accScore += rvol >= rvolLarge ? 1 : 0
accScore += lowerWick > body ? 1 : 0
accScore += close > open and bodyRatio >= 0.55 ? 1 : 0
accScore += nearSupport or inBuyZone ? 2 : 0
accScore += structureBull ? 1 : 0
accScore += bosBull ? 2 : 0
accScore += candleBullScore
accScore += patternBullBoost ? 2 : 0
accScore -= overextended ? 2 : 0
accScore -= nearResistance and not bosBull ? 1 : 0

int distScore = 0
distScore += clv <= 0.45 ? 1 : 0
distScore += clv <= 0.30 ? 1 : 0
distScore += rvol >= 1.20 ? 1 : 0
distScore += rvol >= rvolMedium ? 1 : 0
distScore += rvol >= rvolLarge ? 1 : 0
distScore += upperWick > body ? 1 : 0
distScore += close < open and bodyRatio >= 0.55 ? 1 : 0
distScore += nearResistance ? 2 : 0
distScore += overextended ? 1 : 0
distScore += lh ? 1 : 0
distScore += bosBear ? 2 : 0
distScore += candleBearScore
distScore += (patBiasDir == -1 and patBiasAge <= patBoostBars) ? 2 : 0
distScore -= nearSupport and not bosBear ? 1 : 0

accClass = accScore >= 8 and rvol >= rvolLarge ? 3 : accScore >= 5 and rvol >= rvolMedium ? 2 : accScore >= 3 and rvol >= rvolSmall ? 1 : 0
distClass = distScore >= 8 and rvol >= rvolLarge ? 3 : distScore >= 5 and rvol >= rvolMedium ? 2 : distScore >= 3 and rvol >= rvolSmall ? 1 : 0

absorptionBull = rvol >= rvolLarge and bodyRatio < 0.35 and lowerWick > body and clv >= 0.55 and nearSupport
absorptionBear = rvol >= rvolLarge and bodyRatio < 0.35 and upperWick > body and clv <= 0.45 and nearResistance
volumeAnomaly = rvol >= rvolAnomaly
churn = rvol >= rvolLarge and bodyRatio < 0.30 and rng <= atr14 * 1.2
wideRangeBull = rng >= atr14 * 1.8 and rvol >= rvolMedium and close > open and clv >= 0.70
wideRangeBear = rng >= atr14 * 1.8 and rvol >= rvolMedium and close < open and clv <= 0.30
accCluster = math.sum(accClass > 0 ? 1.0 : 0.0, 5) >= 2 and not bosBear
distCluster = math.sum(distClass > 0 ? 1.0 : 0.0, 5) >= 2 and not bosBull

// ---------- ML1.3: Bandarmologi — money-flow phase (Chaikin-style CMF)
// confirmed by BOTH traded volume (RVOL) and price velocity (ROC), plus
// Anomali-Trap and Akumulasi/Distribusi Bertahap. A different signal
// (flow direction + speed) than accClass/distClass above (candle/CLV-based)
// — shown alongside it as a second, diagnostic read, not a replacement.
mfmPro = (high - low) != 0 ? ((close - low) - (high - close)) / (high - low) : 0.0
mfvPro = mfmPro * volume
cmfPro = math.sum(mfvPro, cmfLenPro) / math.sum(volume, cmfLenPro)
volHotPro = rvol >= rvolMedium
phaseBiasPro = cmfPro >= 0.05 ? 1 : cmfPro <= -0.05 ? -1 : 0
phaseStrengthPro = volHotPro and veloHotPro ? " KUAT (Vol+Speed)" : (volHotPro or veloHotPro) ? " SEDANG" : ""
phaseTextPro = phaseBiasPro == 1 ? "AKUMULASI" + phaseStrengthPro : phaseBiasPro == -1 ? "DISTRIBUSI" + phaseStrengthPro : "NETRAL"

// Anomali-Trap: a big short-term price move riding on abnormally THIN volume
// — a spike with no real participation, the classic false-breakout/phantom-
// bid trap. Akumulasi/Distribusi Bertahap: the CMF phase above confirmed by
// at/above-average volume while price is NOT moving fast — quiet, still-
// unfolding buying/selling, not a lagging confirmation. Both evaluated on
// the CURRENT bar only, confirmed against the CURRENT running RVOL.
anomalyMovePro = math.abs(close - close[anomalyLookbackPro])
isAnomalyTrapPro = anomalyMovePro > atr14 * anomalyMoveMultPro and rvol < anomalyMaxRvolPro
gradualAccumPro = phaseBiasPro == 1 and rvol >= gradualMinRvolPro and not veloHotPro
gradualDistPro = phaseBiasPro == -1 and rvol >= gradualMinRvolPro and not veloHotPro
gradualTierPro = rvol >= gradualBesarRvolPro ? "BESAR" : rvol >= gradualSedangRvolPro ? "SEDANG" : "KECIL"
bandarmologyAnomalyTxt = isAnomalyTrapPro ? "Anomali-Trap" : "Normal"
bandarmologyVolTxt = gradualAccumPro ? "Akumulasi " + gradualTierPro : gradualDistPro ? "Distribusi " + gradualTierPro : ""
bandarmologyText = bandarmologyAnomalyTxt + (bandarmologyVolTxt == "" ? "" : "  |  " + bandarmologyVolTxt)

// ---------- Elite 20D: setups and traps
breakout = not na(r1) and close > r1 + atr14 * 0.10 and close[1] <= r1 and rvol >= rvolMedium and close > open and closeUpper60 and upperWick <= math.max(body, syminfo.mintick)
barsFromBreakout = ta.barssince(breakout)
retest = not na(r1) and barsFromBreakout >= 1 and barsFromBreakout <= 5 and low <= r1 + atr14 * zoneATR and close > r1 and close > open
pullback = (dailyBullStrong or dailyBullEarly) and structureBull and inBuyZone and close > open and clv >= 0.60 and rvol >= 1.0
reversal = nearSupport and hl and bosBull and rvol >= rvolMedium

barsFromBosBull = ta.barssince(bosBull)
bullTrap = not na(r1) and barsFromBosBull >= 1 and barsFromBosBull <= trapWindow and close < r1 and (rvol >= 1.2 or upperWick > body)
upthrust = not na(r1) and high > r1 and close < r1 and upperWick > body and clv <= 0.35 and rvol >= rvolMedium
bearTrap = not na(s1) and low < s1 and close > s1 and lowerWick > body and rvol >= 1.2
gapTrap = not na(r1) and open > r1 and close < r1 and clv <= 0.35 and rvol >= rvolMedium
exhaustion = extensionATR > maxExtensionATR and rsi14 > 75 and rvol >= rvolLarge and (wideRangeBull or upperWick > body)
trapText = bullTrap ? "BTRAP" : bearTrap ? "BRTRAP" : upthrust ? "UT" : gapTrap ? "GTRAP" : exhaustion ? "EXH" : churn ? "CHURN" : volumeAnomaly ? "V!" : "NONE"

// Reversal confluence — catches a fresh bounce off support/lows before the
// weekly trend gate (which lags) turns bullish. Independent of weeklyAllowed/trendAllowed.
reversalConfluence = liquid and (nearSupport or patBiasDir == 1) and candleBullScore >= 2 and rvol >= rvolMedium and not bullTrap and not overextended

// ---------- Elite 20D: entry, stop, targets and sizing
setupCode = retest ? "RT" : pullback ? "PB" : breakout ? "BO" : reversal ? "RV" : reversalConfluence ? "RV2" : "NONE"
candidateEntry = close
autoStopBase = retest ? math.min(low, nz(r1, low)) : breakout ? math.min(low, nz(r1, low)) : nz(s1, low)
autoStop = autoStopBase - stopBufferATR * atr14
candidateRisk = math.max(candidateEntry - autoStop, syminfo.mintick)
stopPct = candidateRisk / candidateEntry * 100
candidateTP1 = candidateEntry + candidateRisk * 1.5
candidateTP2 = candidateEntry + candidateRisk * 2.0
candidateTP3 = candidateEntry + candidateRisk * 3.0
rrToR1 = not na(r1) and r1 > candidateEntry ? (r1 - candidateEntry) / candidateRisk : na
rrToR2 = not na(r2) and r2 > candidateEntry ? (r2 - candidateEntry) / candidateRisk : na
// ML1.0: unknown resistance used to fall back to a 99.0 sentinel that made
// rrOK auto-pass ("not observed" treated as "abundant R:R available"). Now
// an unmeasured R:R space is na and rrOK correctly requires a real,known
// ratio (research_v24/AUDIT.md item 12).
rrAvailable = not na(rrToR1) and not na(rrToR2) ? math.min(rrToR1, rrToR2) : not na(rrToR1) ? rrToR1 : not na(rrToR2) ? rrToR2 : na
rrOK = not na(rrAvailable) and rrAvailable >= minRR
stopOK = autoStop < candidateEntry and stopPct <= maxStopPct
riskRupiah = capital * riskPct / 100
sharesRaw = candidateRisk > 0 ? math.floor(riskRupiah / candidateRisk) : 0
lotsByRisk = math.floor(sharesRaw / 100)
// ML1.0: risk-based sizing alone had no capital ceiling — a tight stop could
// imply a buy larger than available capital (research_v24/AUDIT.md item 3).
// Cap to what `capital` can actually buy at the candidate entry price.
maxLotsByCapital = candidateEntry > 0 ? math.floor(capital / (candidateEntry * 100)) : 0
lots = math.min(lotsByRisk, maxLotsByCapital)

// ---------- ML1.3: independent 0-100 Bull/Bear score + A-F grade
// (bullScorePro/bearScorePro/gradePro) — NOT mutually exclusive (both can be
// low in a genuine range, unlike the single buyScore/10 below). Built from
// every module already computed above (trend, structure, MTF/market/sector,
// bandarmologi, pattern bias, breakout/retest, candle, RSI, ADX, RVOL,
// liquidity, R:R) with a trap-based penalty — the same construction v6.2.2
// validated. Diagnostic only — does NOT gate buySignal/hardGates (see
// header). v6.2.2's own AI-forecast-agreement term (~4 pts) is intentionally
// omitted: this script's AI Forecast is computed later in the file, and
// reordering large existing sections for a 4-point weight isn't worth the
// diff risk. Reuses patBiasDir/breakout/retest/traps/candleBull-BearScore/
// rrAvailable — no recomputation of anything already available above.
f_hasFormingPro(int dir) =>
    found = false
    if array.size(pats) > 0
        for pfi = 0 to array.size(pats) - 1
            pf = array.get(pats, pfi)
            if not pf.confirmed and pf.dir == dir
                found := true
    found
bullFormingPro = f_hasFormingPro(1)
bearFormingPro = f_hasFormingPro(-1)

float bullScorePro = 5.0
float bearScorePro = 5.0
bullScorePro += dailyBullStrong ? 20 : dailyBullEarly ? 12 : 0
bearScorePro += dailyBear ? 20 : 0
bullScorePro += (hh and hl) ? 15 : (not hh and hl) ? 7 : 0
bearScorePro += (lh and ll) ? 15 : (lh and not ll) ? 7 : 0
bullScorePro += mtfBias == 1 ? 10 : 0
bearScorePro += mtfBias == -1 ? 10 : 0
bullScorePro += marketBias == 1 ? 8 : marketBias == 0 ? 3 : 0
bearScorePro += marketBias == -1 ? 8 : marketBias == 0 ? 3 : 0
bullScorePro += rsBias == 1 ? 6 : not useSectorRS ? 3 : 0
bearScorePro += rsBias == -1 ? 6 : not useSectorRS ? 3 : 0
bullScorePro += phaseBiasPro == 1 ? (volHotPro and veloHotPro ? 8 : 5) : 0
bearScorePro += phaseBiasPro == -1 ? (volHotPro and veloHotPro ? 8 : 5) : 0
bullScorePro += patBiasDir == 1 ? 12 : bullFormingPro ? 4 : 0
bearScorePro += patBiasDir == -1 ? 12 : bearFormingPro ? 4 : 0
bullScorePro += breakout ? 12 : retest ? 10 : 0
bearScorePro += bosBear ? 12 : bearTrap ? 6 : 0
bullScorePro += candleBullScore >= 2 ? 5 : 0
bearScorePro += candleBearScore >= 2 ? 5 : 0
bullScorePro += rsi14 >= 50 and rsi14 <= 72 ? 5 : rsi14 > 72 and rsi14 < 80 ? 2 : 0
bearScorePro += rsi14 <= 50 and rsi14 >= 28 ? 5 : rsi14 < 28 and rsi14 > 20 ? 2 : 0
bullScorePro += adx14 >= adxTrendTh and diPlus > diMinus ? (adx14 >= adxStrongTh ? 7 : 5) : adx14 < adxTrendTh and close > ema20 ? 2 : 0
bearScorePro += adx14 >= adxTrendTh and diMinus > diPlus ? (adx14 >= adxStrongTh ? 7 : 5) : adx14 < adxTrendTh and close < ema20 ? 2 : 0
bullScorePro += rvol >= rvolMedium ? 3 : rvol >= minRvol ? 1 : 0
bearScorePro += rvol >= rvolMedium ? 3 : rvol >= minRvol ? 1 : 0
bullScorePro += liquid ? 2 : 0
bearScorePro += liquid ? 2 : 0
bullScorePro -= (bullTrap or upthrust or gapTrap) ? 18 : rsi14 >= 82 ? 6 : 0
bearScorePro -= bearTrap ? 18 : rsi14 <= 18 ? 6 : 0
bullScorePro := f_clamp(bullScorePro, 0, 100)
bearScorePro := f_clamp(bearScorePro, 0, 100)
scoreEdgePro = bullScorePro - bearScorePro
neutralScorePro = f_clamp(100 - math.max(bullScorePro, bearScorePro), 0, 100)

f_gradePro(float score, float rr, bool liq, bool confirmed) =>
    not confirmed ? (score >= setupThresholdPro ? "B — WAIT" : "D — NO TRADE") :
     score >= primeThresholdPro and rr >= 2.0 and liq ? "A+ — PRIME" :
     score >= confirmThresholdPro and rr >= minRR ? "A — HIGH QUALITY" :
     score >= setupThresholdPro ? "B — TRADABLE" : "C — SPECULATIVE"

momentumScore = (rsi14 > 50 ? 1 : 0) + (rsi14 > rsi14[1] ? 1 : 0) + (macdHist > macdHist[1] ? 1 : 0) + (diPlus > diMinus ? 1 : 0)
weeklyAllowed = not wBear
trendAllowed = dailyBullStrong or dailyBullEarly
setupValid = breakout or retest or pullback or reversal
accConfirmed = accClass >= 2 or accCluster or breakout
hardGates = liquid and weeklyAllowed and trendAllowed and (structureBull or bosBull) and setupValid and accConfirmed and momentumScore >= 2 and not overextended and not bullTrap and not upthrust and not gapTrap and rrOK and stopOK and not patternBearBlock and barstate.isconfirmed

int buyScore = 0
buyScore += wBull ? 1 : 0
buyScore += dailyBullStrong ? 2 : dailyBullEarly ? 1 : 0
buyScore += structureBull ? 2 : 0
buyScore += inBuyZone or retest ? 1 : 0
buyScore += setupValid ? 1 : 0
buyScore += rvol >= 1.2 ? 1 : 0
buyScore += momentumScore >= 2 ? 1 : 0
buyScore += rrOK ? 1 : 0
buyScore += candleBullScore >= 2 ? 1 : 0

// buySignalCore is the original trend-following path; buySignalReversal is the
// counter-trend path that does not require weeklyAllowed/trendAllowed — it fires
// on support + bullish candlestick + volume confluence instead.
buySignalCore = hardGates and buyScore >= 8
buySignalReversal = not buySignalCore and reversalConfluence and rrOK and stopOK and not upthrust and not gapTrap and not patternBearBlock and barstate.isconfirmed
buySignal = buySignalCore or buySignalReversal
preBuy = not buySignal and liquid and weeklyAllowed and trendAllowed and structureBull and (accClass >= 2 or accCluster) and not overextended and not bullTrap

// ML1.3: grade needs buySignal (just above) as its "confirmed" flag — placed
// here, right after, rather than beside bullScorePro/bearScorePro above.
gradeActiveScorePro = bullScorePro >= bearScorePro ? bullScorePro : bearScorePro
gradePro = f_gradePro(gradeActiveScorePro, nz(rrAvailable, 0), liquid, buySignal)

// ---------- Elite 20D: owned-position management
// ML1.0: entryPrice/initialStop now FREEZE at the entry event instead of
// recomputing from live s1/ATR every bar, and trailStop only ratchets
// upward — previously both the anchor and the trail could silently drift
// (or fall) while a position stayed open (research_v24/AUDIT.md item 2).
// Both reset to na on exit so the next entry starts clean.
entryPriceLive = avgBuy > 0 ? avgBuy : candidateEntry
ownedAutoStopLive = nz(s1, entryPriceLive - atr14 * 2) - stopBufferATR * atr14
initialStopLive = initialStopInput > 0 ? initialStopInput : ownedAutoStopLive
entryEvent = hasPosition and time[1] < entryTime and time >= entryTime
var float entryPrice = na
var float initialStop = na
if hasPosition and (entryEvent or na(entryPrice))
    entryPrice := entryPriceLive
    initialStop := initialStopLive
else if not hasPosition
    entryPrice := na
    initialStop := na
var float highestSinceEntry = na
inDateWindow = time >= entryTime
if hasPosition and inDateWindow
    highestSinceEntry := na(highestSinceEntry) ? close : math.max(highestSinceEntry, close)
else
    highestSinceEntry := na
atrTrail = nz(highestSinceEntry, close) - 2.0 * atr14
structureTrail = nz(s1, initialStop) - stopBufferATR * atr14
var float trailStop = na
if hasPosition
    trailStopCandidate = math.max(initialStop, math.max(atrTrail, structureTrail))
    trailStop := na(trailStop) ? trailStopCandidate : math.max(trailStop, trailStopCandidate)
else
    trailStop := na
barsSinceEntry = ta.barssince(time[1] < entryTime and time >= entryTime)
barsHeld = hasPosition and inDateWindow ? barsSinceEntry : 0
positionRisk = math.max(entryPrice - initialStop, syminfo.mintick)
ownedTP1 = entryPrice + positionRisk * 1.5
ownedTP2 = entryPrice + positionRisk * 2.0
ownedTP3 = entryPrice + positionRisk * 3.0
hardStopHit = hasPosition and low <= initialStop
trailStopHit = hasPosition and close <= trailStop and trailStop > initialStop
structureExit = hasPosition and bosBear and close < nz(s1, close)
falseBreakExit = hasPosition and bullTrap
tp1Hit = hasPosition and high >= ownedTP1 and high[1] < ownedTP1
tp2Hit = hasPosition and high >= ownedTP2 and high[1] < ownedTP2
tp3Hit = hasPosition and high >= ownedTP3 and high[1] < ownedTP3
reduce50 = hasPosition and distClass >= 3 and (distCluster or momentumScore <= 1)
reduce25 = hasPosition and not reduce50 and distClass >= 2 and (distCluster or momentumScore <= 2)
timeExit = hasPosition and barsHeld >= 20 and close < ownedTP1
lowProgress = hasPosition and barsHeld >= 10 and close < entryPrice + positionRisk * 0.5

// ---------- Elite 20D: single final decision (priority prevents contradictory callbacks)
string decision = "SCAN"
if hasPosition
    decision := hardStopHit ? "CL" : trailStopHit ? "TSTOP-X" : structureExit ? "BOS-X" : falseBreakExit ? "FBO-X" : tp3Hit ? "TP-FINAL" : tp2Hit ? "TP2" : tp1Hit ? "TP1" : reduce50 ? "RED50" : reduce25 ? "RED25" : timeExit ? "TIME-X" : lowProgress ? "HOLD?" : "HOLD"
else
    // ML1.0: buySignalReversal (RV2) is explicitly allowed to fire countertrend
    // (it doesn't require weeklyAllowed/trendAllowed) but the weekly/daily bear
    // check below used to run first, so the panel could show WAIT-T on the
    // very same bar the entry label/alert fired — 47 of 160 BUY signals
    // conflicted with the panel in the walk-forward backtest
    // (research_v24/AUDIT.md item 1). Checking the reversal path first makes
    // the panel agree with whichever signal actually fired.
    decision := not liquid ? "NO-T" : buySignalReversal and rrOK and stopOK ? "BUY-" + setupCode : wBear or dailyBear ? "WAIT-T" : bullTrap or upthrust or gapTrap ? "NO-BUY" : overextended ? "EXT" : not structureBull and not reversalConfluence ? "WAIT-S" : not setupValid and not reversalConfluence ? (preBuy ? "PRE-BUY" : "WAIT-Z") : not rrOK or not stopOK ? "NO-RR" : buySignal ? "BUY-" + setupCode : "WAIT-V"

// ---------- ML1.0: Decision Gate — plain-language execution recommendation.
// dailyBullStrong ("STRONG TREND") and breakout are the two flags this
// script's own out-of-sample event study found with a real, measurable edge
// (10D big-move hit rate 20.2% / 18.0% vs a 15.8% baseline — see
// SCORECARD_AND_RECOMMENDATIONS_ML1.0.md section 2). This block does not add
// a new gate on top of buySignal/exit logic; it translates whichever setup
// already fired into plain BUY/SELL execution language, and separately
// surfaces whether the two validated flags are the ones currently active.
f_buyStyle(string code) =>
    code == "BO" ? "Breakout Buy" : code == "RT" ? "Trailing Buy" : code == "PB" or code == "RV" or code == "RV2" ? "Buy the Dip" : "Buy"

// Same priority order as the `decision` ternary above, bucketed into the
// three requested exit categories (structureExit/falseBreakExit are risk
// exits, so they bucket into "Stop Loss" alongside the hard stop).
sellStyleNow = hardStopHit ? "Stop Loss" : trailStopHit ? "Trailing Stop" : structureExit ? "Stop Loss" : falseBreakExit ? "Stop Loss" : tp3Hit ? "Take Profit" : tp2Hit ? "Take Profit" : tp1Hit ? "Take Profit" : na
sellPriceNow = hardStopHit ? initialStop : trailStopHit ? trailStop : structureExit ? close : falseBreakExit ? close : tp3Hit ? ownedTP3 : tp2Hit ? ownedTP2 : tp1Hit ? ownedTP1 : na
buyStyleNow = f_buyStyle(setupCode)
leadingGate = dailyBullStrong ? "STRONG TREND" : breakout ? "BREAKOUT" : "-"

gateSide = hasPosition ? (not na(sellStyleNow) ? "SELL" : "HOLD") : (buySignal ? "BUY" : "WAIT")
gateStyle = gateSide == "SELL" ? sellStyleNow : gateSide == "BUY" ? buyStyleNow : na
gatePrice = gateSide == "SELL" ? sellPriceNow : gateSide == "BUY" ? candidateEntry : na
gateColor = gateSide == "BUY" ? bullCol : gateSide == "SELL" ? bearCol : color.gray
gateText = not na(gateStyle) ? gateSide + " = " + gateStyle + " : " + str.tostring(gatePrice, format.mintick) : gateSide

// ---------- Entry-Buy / Exit-Sell annotations, reusing the decision engine above.
// Diagonal reference line follows the prior swing pivot into the signal bar, width 2,
// colored bullish/bearish to match the trend direction (bullCol/bearCol reused from
// the Chart Pattern style inputs so the whole script shares one color language).
var line[] sigLines = array.new<line>()
var label[] sigLabels = array.new<label>()
f_capSig() =>
    if array.size(sigLines) > 40
        line.delete(array.shift(sigLines))
    if array.size(sigLabels) > 40
        label.delete(array.shift(sigLabels))

entrySignal = buySignal and barstate.isconfirmed
exitSignal = hasPosition and (hardStopHit or structureExit or falseBreakExit or trailStopHit) and barstate.isconfirmed

if entrySignal
    lbE = label.new(bar_index, low, "ENTRY-BUY: " + str.tostring(candidateEntry, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_up, color = color.new(bullCol, notationTransparency), textcolor = color.new(color.black, 10), size = size.tiny)
    array.push(sigLabels, lbE)
    if not na(lastPLBar)
        lnE = line.new(lastPLBar, lastPL, bar_index, close, color = bullCol, width = 2)
        array.push(sigLines, lnE)
    f_capSig()

if exitSignal
    lbX = label.new(bar_index, high, "EXIT-SELL: " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick), style = label.style_label_down, color = color.new(bearCol, notationTransparency), textcolor = color.new(color.black, 10), size = size.tiny)
    array.push(sigLabels, lbX)
    if not na(lastPHBar)
        lnX = line.new(lastPHBar, lastPH, bar_index, close, color = bearCol, width = 2)
        array.push(sigLines, lnX)
    f_capSig()

// ============================================================================
// ---------- IDX AI + Trend Forecast module ----------
// ============================================================================
// f_clamp used to be defined here — moved up next to f_bold (see the FIX note there) so PRO blocks earlier in the file can call it too.
f_trendPathTarget(_base, _drift, _atr, _horizon) =>
    projected = _base
    for step = 1 to _horizon
        decay = 1.0 - 0.35 * (step - 1) / math.max(_horizon - 1, 1)
        cycle = math.sin(step * 1.618) * _atr * 0.10
        projected := math.max(syminfo.mintick, projected + _drift * decay + cycle)
    projected
// ML1.0: true prefix of the main TR path — keeps the FULL-horizon decay
// denominator (so it decays exactly like the main path) but only walks
// `_steps` iterations, instead of re-deriving with `_horizon` substituted
// for both the loop count and the decay denominator (that substitution
// changed the decay curve itself — research_v24/AUDIT.md item 5; mirrors
// research_v24/engine.py's trend_path(steps=) reference implementation).
// Used for TR1 below. Verified ~zero accuracy delta vs the old approximation
// (research_v24/results/tr1.csv) — this is a correctness/consistency fix,
// not a performance one.
f_trendPathPrefix(_base, _drift, _atr, _fullHorizon, _steps) =>
    projected = _base
    for step = 1 to _steps
        decay = 1.0 - 0.35 * (step - 1) / math.max(_fullHorizon - 1, 1)
        cycle = math.sin(step * 1.618) * _atr * 0.10
        projected := math.max(syminfo.mintick, projected + _drift * decay + cycle)
    projected
f_driftForPathTarget(_base, _target, _atr, _horizon) =>
    decaySum = 0.0
    cycleSum = 0.0
    for step = 1 to _horizon
        decaySum += 1.0 - 0.35 * (step - 1) / math.max(_horizon - 1, 1)
        cycleSum += math.sin(step * 1.618) * _atr * 0.10
    (_target - _base - cycleSum) / math.max(decaySum, 0.01)

regNow = ta.linreg(close, regLen, 0)
regPrev = ta.linreg(close, regLen, 1)
regSlope = regNow - regPrev

// Weekly regime reused directly from wBull/wBear above — not recomputed.
wRegime = wBull ? 1.0 : wBear ? -1.0 : 0.0

trendNorm = atr14 > 0 ? f_clamp(regSlope / atr14, -0.35, 0.35) : 0.0
emaTrend = atr14 > 0 ? f_clamp((ema20 - ema20[5]) / (5 * atr14), -0.35, 0.35) : 0.0
trendComponent = (trendNorm * 0.65 + emaTrend * 0.35 + wRegime * 0.08) * atr14
momentumComponent = f_clamp((rsi14 - 50) / 50, -0.5, 0.5) * atr14 * 0.35

buyPressure = clv >= 0.65 and rvol >= minRvol ? 1.0 : lowerWick > body and clv >= 0.55 ? 0.5 : 0.0
sellPressure = clv <= 0.35 and rvol >= minRvol ? 1.0 : upperWick > body and clv <= 0.45 ? 0.5 : 0.0
flowRaw = f_clamp(buyPressure - sellPressure, -1.0, 1.0)
volumeComponent = flowRaw * atr14 * f_clamp(rvol, 0.5, 2.5) * 0.16
meanRevComponent = (ema20 - close) / math.max(regLen, 1)

// ---------- AI Forecast — pencocokan pola historis
// Mencari N bar terakhir yang paling mirip dengan pola-pola historis (body,
// range, wick atas/bawah dinormalisasi ATR), lalu mengambil rata-rata return
// horizon-bar yang benar-benar terjadi setelah pola-pola analog tersebut.
// (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 — see license note in file header; internals unmodified.)
enum izaDictInput
    bodyF
    crangeF
    wickLowF
    wickHighF

var aiForecastY  = array.new<float>()
var aiForecastD1 = matrix.new<float>()
var aiForecastD2 = matrix.new<float>()
var aiForecastD3 = matrix.new<float>()
var aiForecastD4 = matrix.new<float>()
var aiForecastH  = matrix.new<float>()
var aiForecastL  = matrix.new<float>()
var aiForecastO  = matrix.new<float>()
var aiForecastC  = matrix.new<float>()

var float aiForecastYhat    = na
var float aiForecastConf    = na
var float aiForecastDisp    = na
var int   aiForecastNearest = int(na)

aiForecastAtrNorm = ta.atr(100)
aiForecastN = aiForecastPatternLen
aiForecastNY = horizon
aiForecastNTotal = aiForecastNY + aiForecastN

f_aiForecastUpdateDict(mtx, kind) =>
    x = array.new<float>(aiForecastNTotal)
    for i = 0 to aiForecastNTotal - 1
        if kind == izaDictInput.bodyF
            array.set(x, -(i + 1), close[i] - open[i])
        else if kind == izaDictInput.crangeF
            array.set(x, -(i + 1), high[i] - low[i])
        else if kind == izaDictInput.wickLowF
            array.set(x, -(i + 1), math.min(close[i], open[i]) - low[i])
        else
            array.set(x, -(i + 1), high[i] - math.max(close[i], open[i]))
    xCurrent = array.slice(x, aiForecastNTotal - aiForecastN, aiForecastNTotal)
    xPrev = array.slice(x, 0, aiForecastN)
    xCurrentNormed = matrix.new<float>(1, array.size(xCurrent), 0.0)
    for i = 0 to array.size(xCurrent) - 1
        matrix.set(xCurrentNormed, 0, i, array.get(xCurrent, i) / aiForecastAtrNorm)
    xPrevNormed = array.new<float>(array.size(xPrev), 0.0)
    for i = 0 to array.size(xPrev) - 1
        array.set(xPrevNormed, i, array.get(xPrev, i) / aiForecastAtrNorm)
    if mtx.rows() >= aiForecastDictSize
        mtx.remove_row(0)
    mtx.add_row(mtx.rows(), xPrevNormed)
    xCurrentNormed

f_aiForecastUpdateHist(mtx, sourceSeries) =>
    x = array.new<float>(aiForecastNTotal)
    for i = 0 to aiForecastNTotal - 1
        array.set(x, -(i + 1), sourceSeries[i])
    // Store the realized forward path after the matched pattern, not the
    // pattern itself. This makes visual forecast candles auditable against its target.
    xSeg = array.slice(x, aiForecastN, aiForecastNTotal)
    if mtx.rows() >= aiForecastDictSize
        mtx.remove_row(0)
    mtx.add_row(mtx.rows(), xSeg)

f_aiForecastDistance(x1, x2, x3, x4, d1, d2, d3, d4) =>
    dist = array.new<float>(d1.rows(), 0.0)
    for i = 0 to d1.rows() - 1
        diff1 = x1.diff(d1.submatrix(i, i + 1)).row(0)
        diff2 = x2.diff(d2.submatrix(i, i + 1)).row(0)
        diff3 = x3.diff(d3.submatrix(i, i + 1)).row(0)
        diff4 = x4.diff(d4.submatrix(i, i + 1)).row(0)
        sum = 0.0
        for j = 0 to aiForecastN - 1
            sum += math.pow(diff1.get(j), 2) * 0.25 + math.pow(diff2.get(j), 2) * 0.25 + math.pow(diff3.get(j), 2) * 0.25 + math.pow(diff4.get(j), 2) * 0.25
        dist.set(i, math.sqrt(sum))
    dist

f_aiForecastPredict(dist, yArr, nNeighbors, minSpacing, weightPower) =>
    idx = dist.sort_indices()
    selected = array.new<int>()
    // Greedy de-correlation: do not let a cluster of overlapping windows
    // masquerade as several independent neighbors.
    if idx.size() > 0
        for i = 0 to idx.size() - 1
            candidate = idx.get(i)
            eligible = true
            if selected.size() > 0
                for j = 0 to selected.size() - 1
                    if math.abs(candidate - selected.get(j)) < minSpacing
                        eligible := false
            if eligible and selected.size() < nNeighbors
                selected.push(candidate)
    n = selected.size()
    eps = 1e-6
    weightSumLocal = 0.0
    weightedRet = 0.0
    weightedUp = 0.0
    if n > 0
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            id = selected.get(i)
            w = 1.0 / math.pow(math.max(dist.get(id), eps), weightPower)
            weightSumLocal += w
            weightedRet += yArr.get(id) * w
            weightedUp += (yArr.get(id) > 0 ? 1.0 : 0.0) * w
    avg = weightSumLocal > 0 ? weightedRet / weightSumLocal : 0.0
    variance = 0.0
    if n > 0 and weightSumLocal > 0
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            id = selected.get(i)
            w = 1.0 / math.pow(math.max(dist.get(id), eps), weightPower)
            variance += w * math.pow(yArr.get(id) - avg, 2)
        variance /= weightSumLocal
    dispersion = math.sqrt(variance)
    directionVote = weightSumLocal > 0 ? math.max(weightedUp / weightSumLocal, 1.0 - weightedUp / weightSumLocal) : 0.5
    nearestDistance = n > 0 ? dist.get(selected.get(0)) : na
    distanceQuality = not na(nearestDistance) ? math.exp(-nearestDistance / math.sqrt(aiForecastN)) : 0.0
    stability = math.exp(-dispersion * 8.0)
    // ML1.0 note: same caveat as TR confidence above — this is a heuristic
    // vote/quality/stability blend, not a calibrated probability. A single
    // identical neighbor with zero dispersion can score ~100% with no
    // evidence of a matching realized hit rate (research_v24/AUDIT.md item 4).
    robustConfidence = f_clamp(0.5 * directionVote + 0.3 * distanceQuality + 0.2 * stability, 0.0, 1.0)
    [avg, robustConfidence, n > 0 ? selected.get(0) : int(na), dispersion]

// ML1.0: gate also waits for ta.atr(100) (aiForecastAtrNorm) to have enough
// bars to be valid — the old bar_index > aiForecastNTotal gate (~40 bars by
// default) could open before bar 99, letting the dictionary normalize by an
// immature ATR(100) (research_v24/AUDIT.md item 11).
if useaiForecast and barstate.isconfirmed and bar_index > math.max(aiForecastNTotal, 100)
    rawYLabel = math.log(close) - math.log(close[aiForecastNY])
    // Winsorize extreme events so one gap/crash cannot dominate the analog set.
    yLabel = f_clamp(rawYLabel, math.log(1.0 - maxForecastPct / 100.0), math.log(1.0 + maxForecastPct / 100.0))
    xBody = f_aiForecastUpdateDict(aiForecastD1, izaDictInput.bodyF)
    xRange = f_aiForecastUpdateDict(aiForecastD2, izaDictInput.crangeF)
    xWickLow = f_aiForecastUpdateDict(aiForecastD3, izaDictInput.wickLowF)
    xWickHigh = f_aiForecastUpdateDict(aiForecastD4, izaDictInput.wickHighF)
    f_aiForecastUpdateHist(aiForecastH, high)
    f_aiForecastUpdateHist(aiForecastL, low)
    f_aiForecastUpdateHist(aiForecastO, open)
    f_aiForecastUpdateHist(aiForecastC, close)
    if aiForecastY.size() >= aiForecastDictSize
        aiForecastY.shift()
    aiForecastY.push(yLabel)
    dist = f_aiForecastDistance(xBody, xRange, xWickLow, xWickHigh, aiForecastD1, aiForecastD2, aiForecastD3, aiForecastD4)
    [avgRet, confRatio, nearestIdx, dispersion] = f_aiForecastPredict(dist, aiForecastY, aiForecastNeighbors, aiForecastMinSpacing, aiForecastWeightPower)
    aiForecastYhat := avgRet
    aiForecastConf := confRatio
    aiForecastNearest := nearestIdx
    aiForecastDisp := dispersion

// ML1.0: aiForecastYhat is shrunk toward zero (aiShrink, default 0.25) before
// filtering into a price target — research_v24 found this cuts out-of-sample
// MAE ~20% vs the raw forecast. Magnitude calibration only, not a directional
// improvement (see MODEL VALIDATION NOTES in the file header).
aiForecastYhatFiltered = ta.ema(aiForecastYhat, aiForecastFilterLen) * aiShrink
aiForecastForecastClose = not na(aiForecastYhatFiltered) ? close * math.exp(aiForecastYhatFiltered) : na
aiForecastDailyDrift = not na(aiForecastForecastClose) ? (aiForecastForecastClose - close) / horizon : na

weightSum = math.max(wTrend + wMomentum + wVolume + wMeanRev, 0.01)
dailyDriftRaw = (wTrend * trendComponent + wMomentum * momentumComponent + wVolume * volumeComponent + wMeanRev * meanRevComponent) / weightSum
maxDailyMove = close * (maxForecastPct / 100) / horizon
// ML1.0: same shrink treatment (trShrink, default 0.25) applied to the TR
// ensemble drift — see aiShrink note above.
dailyDriftEnsemble = f_clamp(dailyDriftRaw, -maxDailyMove, maxDailyMove) * trShrink
aiForecastDailyDriftClamped = not na(aiForecastDailyDrift) ? f_clamp(aiForecastDailyDrift, -maxDailyMove, maxDailyMove) : na
// The user-set weight is a ceiling. Weak or dispersed matches automatically
// receive less influence instead of forcing a low-quality analog into the blend.
aiForecastActiveWeight = useaiForecast and not na(aiForecastDailyDriftClamped) ? aiForecastWeight * f_clamp(0.25 + 0.75 * nz(aiForecastConf, 0.0), 0.0, 1.0) : 0.0
trendModelTarget = f_trendPathTarget(close, dailyDriftEnsemble, atr14, horizon)
// Benchmark winner: adaptive terminal-target blend. Then solve the per-candle
// drift so the final TR candle closes exactly at the displayed target.
trendForecastClose20 = trendModelTarget * (1.0 - aiForecastActiveWeight) + nz(aiForecastForecastClose, trendModelTarget) * aiForecastActiveWeight
dailyDrift = f_driftForPathTarget(close, trendForecastClose20, atr14, horizon)
forecastPct = (trendForecastClose20 / close - 1) * 100

trendAgree = math.sign(regSlope) == math.sign(ema20 - ema50) ? 1.0 : 0.0
weeklyAgree = math.sign(dailyDrift) == math.sign(wRegime) or wRegime == 0 ? 1.0 : 0.0
volumeAgree = rvol >= minRvol and math.sign(flowRaw) == math.sign(dailyDrift) ? 1.0 : 0.0
structureQuality = close > sma200 and ema20 > ema50 ? 1.0 : close < sma200 and ema20 < ema50 ? 1.0 : 0.4
aiForecastAgree = useaiForecast and not na(aiForecastDailyDriftClamped) ? (math.sign(aiForecastDailyDriftClamped) == math.sign(dailyDriftEnsemble) ? 1.0 : 0.0) : 0.5
aiForecastScore = useaiForecast and not na(aiForecastDailyDriftClamped) ? aiForecastAgree * nz(aiForecastConf, 0.5) : 0.5
// ML1.0 note: this "confidence" is a heuristic rule-agreement score (how many
// independent signals point the same way), NOT a calibrated probability of
// the forecast being correct — a single unanimous, low-dispersion read can
// score high with no evidence it corresponds to a matching realized hit
// rate (research_v24/AUDIT.md item 4). Cross-check TR DIR ACC / TR TOL ACC
// on the dashboard for the realized historical accuracy at this confidence
// level instead of reading this number as a probability on its own.
confidence = f_clamp(38 + trendAgree * 13 + weeklyAgree * 10 + volumeAgree * 10 + structureQuality * 8 + aiForecastScore * 11 - f_clamp(atr14 / close * 100 - 5, 0, 10), 35, 90)
direction = confidence < minConfidence ? "NEUTRAL" : forecastPct > 1 ? "UP" : forecastPct < -1 ? "DOWN" : "SIDEWAYS"
invalidation = dailyDrift >= 0 ? close - atrInvalidation * atr14 : close + atrInvalidation * atr14
aiForecastPct = not na(aiForecastForecastClose) ? (aiForecastForecastClose / close - 1.0) * 100.0 : na
aiForecastDirection = na(aiForecastPct) ? "WAIT" : math.abs(aiForecastPct) <= 1.0 ? "NEUTRAL" : aiForecastPct > 0 ? "UP" : "DOWN"
aiForecastConfidencePct = nz(aiForecastConf) * 100.0
aiForecastInvalidation = nz(aiForecastDailyDriftClamped) >= 0 ? close - atrInvalidation * atr14 : close + atrInvalidation * atr14
aiForecastStatus = not useaiForecast ? "OFF" : na(aiForecastForecastClose) ? "WARMING UP" : aiForecastConfidencePct >= minConfidence ? "VALID" : "LOW CONF"

// ============================================================================
// ML1.4: DECISION GATE 2.0 — evidence-weighted synthesis of every signal this
// script computes, weighted by what has ACTUALLY been measured against
// idx_stocks_10y (see header changelog for the full reasoning). Purely
// additive: leadingGate/gateText/gateSide/decision/buySignal/bullScorePro/
// aiForecastDirection etc. are all read here, none are modified.
// ============================================================================
// Component votes, each scaled to roughly the same 0-30 range so no single
// term can dominate by accident:
//   - Leading flags (dailyBullStrong/breakout/dailyBear): HIGH weight —
//     10D big-move hit rate 20.2%/18.0% vs 15.8% baseline, a REAL measured
//     edge (SCORECARD_AND_RECOMMENDATIONS_ML1.0.md section 2).
//   - Chart Pattern bias (patBiasDir): HIGH weight — DT/DB measured 65.7%/
//     70.8% target-hit rate, the single most validated read in this script.
//   - bullScorePro/bearScorePro (ML1.3): MEDIUM weight — richer context, but
//     UNVALIDATED against this dataset.
//   - TR/AI Forecast direction: LOW weight — PROVEN to have NO directional
//     edge (47-48% accuracy, below the 51.4% naive baseline,
//     research_v24/results/summary.csv). Included only as tie-break context,
//     never as a primary driver — this is the opposite of how most retail
//     scripts (including v6.2.2) weight their own AI forecast.
//   - Bandarmologi Anomali-Trap: a VETO/dampener (halves conviction toward
//     neutral), not a directional vote — a trap should suppress confidence,
//     not add to either side.
componentBullPro = 0.0
componentBearPro = 0.0
componentBullPro += dailyBullStrong ? 30 : breakout ? 24 : dailyBullEarly ? 10 : 0
componentBearPro += dailyBear ? 24 : 0
componentBullPro += patBiasDir == 1 ? 26 : 0
componentBearPro += patBiasDir == -1 ? 26 : 0
componentBullPro += (bullScorePro - 50) * 0.30
componentBearPro += (bearScorePro - 50) * 0.30
componentBullPro += direction == "UP" ? 6 : 0
componentBearPro += direction == "DOWN" ? 6 : 0
componentBullPro += aiForecastDirection == "UP" ? 4 : 0
componentBearPro += aiForecastDirection == "DOWN" ? 4 : 0
trapDampenPro = isAnomalyTrapPro ? 0.5 : 1.0
convictionRawPro = (componentBullPro - componentBearPro) * trapDampenPro
convictionScorePro = f_clamp(50 + convictionRawPro, 0, 100)
convictionAbsPro = math.min(100.0, math.abs(convictionScorePro - 50) * 2)
gate2Dir = convictionScorePro > 54 ? "BUY BIAS" : convictionScorePro < 46 ? "SELL/AVOID BIAS" : "NETRAL"
gate2Tier = convictionAbsPro >= 50 ? "A+ PRIME" : convictionAbsPro >= 30 ? "A HIGH" : convictionAbsPro >= 14 ? "B MODERATE" : "C LOW"

// Conflict flag: leading-flag/pattern evidence (validated) vs AI/TR forecast
// direction (proven no edge) actively disagreeing — surfaced explicitly
// rather than silently averaged away.
leadPatternBullPro = dailyBullStrong or breakout or patBiasDir == 1
leadPatternBearPro = dailyBear or patBiasDir == -1
forecastBullPro = direction == "UP" or aiForecastDirection == "UP"
forecastBearPro = direction == "DOWN" or aiForecastDirection == "DOWN"
conflictFlagPro = (leadPatternBullPro and forecastBearPro) or (leadPatternBearPro and forecastBullPro)

f_gate2Push(arr, cond, txt) =>
    if cond
        array.push(arr, txt)

gate2Parts = array.new<string>()
f_gate2Push(gate2Parts, dailyBullStrong, "Leading:StrongTrend")
f_gate2Push(gate2Parts, not dailyBullStrong and breakout, "Leading:Breakout")
f_gate2Push(gate2Parts, dailyBear, "Leading:Bear")
f_gate2Push(gate2Parts, patBiasDir == 1, "Pattern:Bullish")
f_gate2Push(gate2Parts, patBiasDir == -1, "Pattern:Bearish")
f_gate2Push(gate2Parts, bullScorePro >= 60, "ScorePro:Bull" + str.tostring(bullScorePro, "#"))
f_gate2Push(gate2Parts, bearScorePro >= 60, "ScorePro:Bear" + str.tostring(bearScorePro, "#"))
f_gate2Push(gate2Parts, isAnomalyTrapPro, "⚠Anomali-Trap")
gate2Reason = (array.size(gate2Parts) > 0 ? array.join(gate2Parts, " + ") : "Tidak ada evidence kuat") + (conflictFlagPro ? "  ⚠ vs Forecast (no proven edge)" : "")

// Suggested size = risk-based `lots` (unchanged, still computed above) scaled
// DOWN by conviction tier — standard professional practice (size down on a
// lower-quality read), never scaled UP, and zero outside a BUY-biased read
// since this script's plan (`lots`/`candidateEntry`/`autoStop`) is long-only.
lotsConvictionMultPro = gate2Dir != "BUY BIAS" ? 0.0 : convictionAbsPro >= 50 ? 1.0 : convictionAbsPro >= 30 ? 0.65 : convictionAbsPro >= 14 ? 0.35 : 0.0
lotsConvictionPro = math.floor(lots * lotsConvictionMultPro)

gate2Text = hasPosition ? (not na(sellStyleNow) ? "SELL/EXIT — " + sellStyleNow : "HOLD — " + gate2Dir + " (" + gate2Tier + ")") : isAnomalyTrapPro ? "HINDARI — Anomali-Trap terdeteksi" : gate2Dir == "BUY BIAS" ? "PERTIMBANGKAN BUY — " + gate2Tier + " (lot sugesti: " + str.tostring(lotsConvictionPro) + "/" + str.tostring(lots) + ")" : gate2Dir == "SELL/AVOID BIAS" ? "HINDARI/JANGAN BUY — " + gate2Tier : "NETRAL — tunggu evidence lebih kuat"

// ============================================================================
// DG2.2: DECISION GATE 2.0 TRADE PLAN — the validated "Edge" (see header and
// DG22_EDGE_RESEARCH_RESULTS.md). This is NOT a new entry signal: the entry
// condition (gate2Signal) is the SAME gate2Dir=="BUY BIAS" + tier A+/A/B read
// already used for lotsConvictionPro above. What's new is the EXIT: an ATR
// trailing stop (no fixed R-multiple target) instead of the legacy fixed-2R
// exit, walk-forward validated to cut the average loss per signal from
// -0.52% to -0.09% on held-out data (still net-negative — PF 0.976, not a
// guarantee of profit, just a real, measured improvement).
// Mirrors the EXISTING hasPosition/highestSinceEntry/trailStop mechanism
// structurally (same "ratchet the stop up, never down" pattern) but is a
// FULLY SEPARATE state machine — reads nothing from and writes nothing to
// hasPosition/entryPrice/trailStop/highestSinceEntry, and does not gate or
// alter buySignal/hardGates/decision. Purely a "if you'd taken the last
// Decision Gate 2.0 BUY BIAS signal" hypothetical/informational tracker.
gate2Signal = gate2Dir == "BUY BIAS" and gate2Tier != "C LOW"
var bool  gate2InPlan = false
var float gate2PlanEntry = na
var int   gate2PlanEntryBar = na
var float gate2PlanHighest = na
var float gate2PlanStop = na

gate2NewSignal = gate2Signal and not gate2InPlan and barstate.isconfirmed
if gate2NewSignal
    gate2InPlan := true
    gate2PlanEntry := close
    gate2PlanEntryBar := bar_index
    gate2PlanHighest := close
    gate2PlanStop := autoStop

gate2PlanBarsHeld = gate2InPlan ? bar_index - gate2PlanEntryBar : na
if gate2InPlan
    gate2PlanHighest := math.max(gate2PlanHighest, close)
    if gate2PlanBarsHeld >= gate2MinHoldBars
        gate2PlanStop := math.max(gate2PlanStop, gate2PlanHighest - gate2TrailAtrMult * atr14)

gate2PlanExitHit = gate2InPlan and barstate.isconfirmed and (close <= gate2PlanStop or gate2PlanBarsHeld >= gate2MaxHoldBars)
gate2PlanExitReason = gate2PlanExitHit ? (close <= gate2PlanStop ? "TRAIL STOP" : "MAKS TAHAN") : na
gate2PlanStatusTxt = gate2InPlan ? "AKTIF sejak " + str.tostring(gate2PlanBarsHeld) + " bar (entry " + str.tostring(gate2PlanEntry, format.mintick) + ", trail " + str.tostring(gate2PlanStop, format.mintick) + ")" : "tidak ada plan aktif"
if gate2PlanExitHit
    gate2InPlan := false

// ---------- Locked rolling validation
// Every closed real candle is compared only with the one-step forecast that
// was created at the previous close. This avoids choosing among overlapping
// forecast vintages after the result is known.
nextCycle = math.sin(1.618) * atr14 * 0.10
nextUncertainty = atr14 * (0.45 + 0.055) * (1.15 - confidence / 200)
trendNextPredOpen = close
trendNextPredClose = math.max(syminfo.mintick, close + dailyDrift + nextCycle)
trendNextPredHigh = math.max(trendNextPredOpen, trendNextPredClose) + nextUncertainty * 0.45
trendNextPredLow = math.max(syminfo.mintick, math.min(trendNextPredOpen, trendNextPredClose) - nextUncertainty * 0.45)

lockedOpen = trendNextPredOpen[1]
lockedClose = trendNextPredClose[1]
lockedHigh = trendNextPredHigh[1]
lockedLow = trendNextPredLow[1]
lockedATR = atr14[1]
predMove = lockedClose - lockedOpen
realMove = close - close[1]
flatThreshold = nz(lockedATR) * 0.05
directionMatch = math.abs(predMove) <= flatThreshold ? math.abs(realMove) <= flatThreshold : math.sign(predMove) == math.sign(realMove)
closeError = math.abs(close - lockedClose)
toleranceMatch = closeError <= nz(lockedATR) * errorToleranceATR
validationReady = barstate.isconfirmed and not na(lockedClose) and not na(lockedATR)
validationTrue = validationReady and directionMatch and (evaluationMode == "Direction only" or toleranceMatch)
validationFalse = validationReady and not validationTrue
validationCount = math.sum(validationReady ? 1.0 : 0.0, evaluationLookback)
validationWins = math.sum(validationTrue ? 1.0 : 0.0, evaluationLookback)
accuracy1D = validationCount > 0 ? validationWins / validationCount * 100 : na

// Independent horizon validation: compare today's close with the 20-bar
// target locked exactly `horizon` bars ago. This is displayed as statistics,
// not used to repaint historical candles or alter the live projection.
dueForecast = trendForecastClose20[horizon]
dueBase = close[horizon]
dueATR = atr14[horizon]
validation20Ready = barstate.isconfirmed and not na(dueForecast) and not na(dueBase)
direction20Match = math.sign(dueForecast - dueBase) == math.sign(close - dueBase)
tolerance20Match = math.abs(close - dueForecast) <= nz(dueATR) * math.sqrt(horizon) * errorToleranceATR
validation20True = validation20Ready and direction20Match and (evaluationMode == "Direction only" or tolerance20Match)
validation20Count = math.sum(validation20Ready ? 1.0 : 0.0, evaluationLookback)
validation20Wins = math.sum(validation20True ? 1.0 : 0.0, evaluationLookback)
direction20Wins = math.sum(validation20Ready and direction20Match ? 1.0 : 0.0, evaluationLookback)
target20Wins = math.sum(validation20Ready and tolerance20Match ? 1.0 : 0.0, evaluationLookback)
directionAccuracy20D = validation20Count > 0 ? direction20Wins / validation20Count * 100 : na
accuracy20D = validation20Count > 0 ? target20Wins / validation20Count * 100 : na

dueAiForecast = aiForecastForecastClose[horizon]
aiValidation20Ready = barstate.isconfirmed and not na(dueAiForecast) and not na(dueBase)
aiDirection20Match = math.sign(dueAiForecast - dueBase) == math.sign(close - dueBase)
aiTolerance20Match = math.abs(close - dueAiForecast) <= nz(dueATR) * math.sqrt(horizon) * errorToleranceATR
aiValidation20True = aiValidation20Ready and aiDirection20Match and (evaluationMode == "Direction only" or aiTolerance20Match)
aiValidation20Count = math.sum(aiValidation20Ready ? 1.0 : 0.0, evaluationLookback)
aiValidation20Wins = math.sum(aiValidation20True ? 1.0 : 0.0, evaluationLookback)
aiDirection20Wins = math.sum(aiValidation20Ready and aiDirection20Match ? 1.0 : 0.0, evaluationLookback)
aiTarget20Wins = math.sum(aiValidation20Ready and aiTolerance20Match ? 1.0 : 0.0, evaluationLookback)
aiDirectionAccuracy20D = aiValidation20Count > 0 ? aiDirection20Wins / aiValidation20Count * 100 : na
aiAccuracy20D = aiValidation20Count > 0 ? aiTarget20Wins / aiValidation20Count * 100 : na

// ---------- Short-term (10D) levels — Support/Resistance/TR1/TR2/Stop/Entry, referencing
// the AI/TR Forecast's own range and timeline per explicit request. TR2 reuses
// trendForecastClose20 directly (no recompute); TR1 reuses the same
// f_trendPathTarget/dailyDrift the main forecast already uses, evaluated at a shorter
// horizon so it stays tied to the same forecast path instead of being a separate,
// disconnected calculation.
shortSupport = ta.lowest(low, srLookback)
shortResistance = ta.highest(high, srLookback)
shortStopLoss = shortSupport - stopBufferATR * atr14
tr1Steps = math.min(srLookback, horizon)
// ML1.0: f_trendPathPrefix keeps `horizon` as the decay denominator and only
// walks `tr1Steps` iterations, so TR1 is a genuine prefix of the same TR
// path instead of a separately-decaying short-horizon approximation.
tr1Target = f_trendPathPrefix(close, dailyDrift, atr14, horizon, tr1Steps)
tr2Target = trendForecastClose20
entryArea = candidateEntry

// Accuracy/consistency check for the new short-term levels, using the same locked-
// rolling methodology as the TR/AI forecast validation above.
dueTR1 = tr1Target[srLookback]
tr1ValidReady = barstate.isconfirmed and not na(dueTR1) and not na(close[srLookback])
tr1DirMatch = math.sign(dueTR1 - close[srLookback]) == math.sign(close - close[srLookback])
tr1TolMatch = math.abs(close - dueTR1) <= nz(atr14[srLookback]) * math.sqrt(srLookback) * errorToleranceATR
tr1ValidTrue = tr1ValidReady and tr1DirMatch and (evaluationMode == "Direction only" or tr1TolMatch)
tr1ValidCount = math.sum(tr1ValidReady ? 1.0 : 0.0, evaluationLookback)
tr1ValidWins = math.sum(tr1ValidTrue ? 1.0 : 0.0, evaluationLookback)
tr1Accuracy = tr1ValidCount > 0 ? tr1ValidWins / tr1ValidCount * 100 : na

// Did the 10-bar S/R band set `srLookback` bars ago hold for the ENTIRE
// window since, not just on this one bar? ML1.0: the old endpoint-only test
// reported "held" 48.3% of the time; checking every bar of the actual
// window (as below) it only held 24.8% of the time — the old metric
// overstated level reliability by roughly 2x (research_v24/AUDIT.md item 6,
// research_v24/results/sr_diagnostics.csv). Buffer now uses ATR at the
// window's origin (atr14[srLookback]), not current ATR.
srSupportLocked = shortSupport[srLookback]
srResistanceLocked = shortResistance[srLookback]
srCheckReady = barstate.isconfirmed and not na(srSupportLocked) and not na(srResistanceLocked)
srBuf = nz(atr14[srLookback]) * 0.25
srHeldPath = true
if srCheckReady
    for k = 0 to srLookback - 1
        if low[k] < srSupportLocked - srBuf or high[k] > srResistanceLocked + srBuf
            srHeldPath := false
srHeld = srCheckReady and srHeldPath
srCheckCount = math.sum(srCheckReady ? 1.0 : 0.0, evaluationLookback)
srHeldCount = math.sum(srHeld ? 1.0 : 0.0, evaluationLookback)
srConsistency = srCheckCount > 0 ? srHeldCount / srCheckCount * 100 : na

// Historical locked candles remain on chart automatically as series plots.
lockedMoveATR = nz(lockedATR) > 0 ? (lockedClose - lockedOpen) / lockedATR : 0.0
histColor = color.new(color.silver, 70)
plotcandle(showHistory ? lockedOpen : na, showHistory ? lockedHigh : na, showHistory ? lockedLow : na, showHistory ? lockedClose : na, title="Locked Trend Forecast Candle", color=histColor, wickcolor=histColor, bordercolor=histColor)
// Validation remains active for accuracy statistics; no per-bar result
// notation is drawn on the price chart.

var line[] fcDrawings = array.new<line>()
var label[] fcNotes = array.new<label>()
var box[] aiForecastBoxes = array.new<box>()
f_fcClear() =>
    while array.size(fcDrawings) > 0
        line.delete(array.pop(fcDrawings))
    while array.size(fcNotes) > 0
        label.delete(array.pop(fcNotes))
    while array.size(aiForecastBoxes) > 0
        box.delete(array.pop(aiForecastBoxes))

// Short-term level line + right-end tag: width 1, transparent (lineTransparency /
// notationTransparency), tag text small with the price (plain text — see the
// v2.1 BUG FIX note near panelMsg for why f_bold() is no longer used here).
f_levelLine(endX, priceVal, nameTxt, baseCol, isLight) =>
    array.push(fcDrawings, line.new(bar_index, priceVal, endX, priceVal, xloc=xloc.bar_index, color=color.new(baseCol, lineTransparency), style=line.style_solid, width=1))
    tagTxt = nameTxt + " " + str.tostring(priceVal, format.mintick)
    array.push(fcNotes, label.new(endX, priceVal, tagTxt, xloc=xloc.bar_index, style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(baseCol, notationTransparency), textcolor=color.new(color.black, 10), size=size.tiny))

if barstate.islast
    f_fcClear()
    // Satu forecast candle menempati satu bar, sama seperti candle normal.
    int visualStep = 1
    int commonForecastEnd = bar_index + horizon * visualStep
    // ML1.0: TR Forecast target line extended 5 bars farther (14 -> 19), AI
    // Forecast target line extended 9 bars farther (0 -> 9 past
    // commonForecastEnd) so the two target labels sit further apart.
    int trendTargetEnd = commonForecastEnd + 19
    int aiTargetEnd = commonForecastEnd + 9
    float prevC = close
    float upperPrev = close
    float lowerPrev = close
    for i = 1 to horizon
        decay = 1.0 - 0.35 * (i - 1) / math.max(horizon - 1, 1)
        cycle = math.sin(i * 1.618) * atr14 * 0.10
        predO = prevC
        predC = math.max(syminfo.mintick, predO + dailyDrift * decay + cycle)
        uncertainty = atr14 * (0.45 + 0.055 * i) * (1.15 - confidence / 200)
        predH = math.max(predO, predC) + uncertainty * 0.45
        predL = math.max(syminfo.mintick, math.min(predO, predC) - uncertainty * 0.45)
        stepMoveATR = atr14 > 0 ? (predC - predO) / atr14 : 0.0
        candleColor = stepMoveATR > 0.05 ? color.new(color.lime, 70) : stepMoveATR < -0.05 ? color.new(color.red, 70) : color.new(color.orange, 70)
        candleX = bar_index + i * visualStep
        priorX = i == 1 ? bar_index : bar_index + (i - 1) * visualStep
        if showCandles
            array.push(fcDrawings, line.new(candleX, predL, candleX, predH, xloc=xloc.bar_index, color=candleColor, style=line.style_dashed, width=1))
            array.push(fcDrawings, line.new(candleX, predO, candleX, predC, xloc=xloc.bar_index, color=candleColor, style=line.style_dashed, width=4))
        array.push(fcDrawings, line.new(priorX, prevC, candleX, predC, xloc=xloc.bar_index, color=color.new(color.yellow, 70), style=line.style_dashed, width=2))
        if showBand
            upperNow = predC + uncertainty
            lowerNow = predC - uncertainty
            array.push(fcDrawings, line.new(priorX, upperPrev, candleX, upperNow, xloc=xloc.bar_index, color=color.new(color.gray, 55), style=line.style_dotted))
            array.push(fcDrawings, line.new(priorX, lowerPrev, candleX, lowerNow, xloc=xloc.bar_index, color=color.new(color.gray, 55), style=line.style_dotted))
            upperPrev := upperNow
            lowerPrev := lowerNow
        prevC := predC
    arrowColor = direction == "UP" ? color.new(color.lime, 55) : direction == "DOWN" ? color.new(color.red, 55) : color.new(color.orange, 55)
    trendStatus = confidence >= minConfidence ? "VALID" : "LOW CONF"
    msg = "TR Forecast\n" + direction + " " + str.tostring(horizon) + "D\nTarget: " + str.tostring(trendForecastClose20, format.mintick) + "\n" + str.tostring(forecastPct, "#.##") + "% | Conf " + str.tostring(confidence, "#") + "%\nInvalid: " + str.tostring(invalidation, format.mintick) + "\nStatus: " + trendStatus + "\nTol Acc: " + str.tostring(accuracy20D, "#.##") + "%"
    // Black target line; TR extends nine bars farther to keep panels separate.
    array.push(fcDrawings, line.new(bar_index, trendForecastClose20, trendTargetEnd, trendForecastClose20, xloc=xloc.bar_index, color=color.new(color.black, 70), style=line.style_dashed, width=1))
    // TR directional arrow: dashed trend-colored shaft plus arrow head.
    array.push(fcDrawings, line.new(bar_index, close, commonForecastEnd, trendForecastClose20, xloc=xloc.bar_index, color=color.new(arrowColor, 18), style=line.style_dashed, width=2))
    array.push(fcNotes, label.new(commonForecastEnd, trendForecastClose20, "➤", xloc=xloc.bar_index, style=label.style_none, color=na, textcolor=color.new(color.black, 10), size=size.tiny))
    array.push(fcNotes, label.new(trendTargetEnd, trendForecastClose20, msg, xloc=xloc.bar_index, style=label.style_label_upper_left, color=arrowColor, textcolor=color.new(color.black, 10), size=size.tiny))

    // AI Forecast visual — replays the nearest historical analog's
    // own N-bar shape, rescaled onto the current price, as a secondary cue.
    if showPatternShape and useaiForecast and not na(aiForecastNearest) and aiForecastH.rows() > 0 and aiForecastO.rows() > 0 and aiForecastC.rows() > 0
        patRow = int(math.max(0, math.min(aiForecastNearest, aiForecastH.rows() - 1)))
        patternHigh = aiForecastH.row(patRow)
        patternLow = aiForecastL.row(patRow)
        patternOpen = aiForecastO.row(patRow)
        patternClose = aiForecastC.row(patRow)
        patLen = patternHigh.size()
        if patLen > 1
            shapeHighs = array.new<float>(0)
            shapeLows = array.new<float>(0)
            shapeOpens = array.new<float>(0)
            shapeCloses = array.new<float>(0)
            patternAnchor = math.max(patternOpen.get(0), syminfo.mintick)
            rawFinalClose = math.max((patternClose.get(patLen - 1) / patternAnchor) * close, syminfo.mintick)
            targetScale = aiForecastForecastClose / rawFinalClose
            for i = 0 to patLen - 1
                progress = (i + 1.0) / patLen
                progressiveScale = 1.0 + progress * (targetScale - 1.0)
                array.push(shapeHighs, (patternHigh.get(i) / patternAnchor) * close * progressiveScale)
                array.push(shapeLows, (patternLow.get(i) / patternAnchor) * close * progressiveScale)
                array.push(shapeOpens, (patternOpen.get(i) / patternAnchor) * close * progressiveScale)
                array.push(shapeCloses, (patternClose.get(i) / patternAnchor) * close * progressiveScale)
            shapeSpan = array.size(shapeHighs)
            echoColor = aiForecastDirection == "UP" ? color.new(color.lime, 70) : aiForecastDirection == "DOWN" ? color.new(color.red, 70) : color.new(color.orange, 70)
            // Resample the matched pattern onto the same horizon/timeline used
            // by TR Forecast. Each AI candle is a colored dashed range line.
            for k = 0 to horizon - 1
                sourceIndex = int(math.round(k * (shapeSpan - 1) / math.max(horizon - 1, 1)))
                candleHigh = array.get(shapeHighs, sourceIndex)
                candleLow = array.get(shapeLows, sourceIndex)
                candleOpen = array.get(shapeOpens, sourceIndex)
                candleClose = array.get(shapeCloses, sourceIndex)
                candleMove = atr14 > 0 ? (candleClose - candleOpen) / atr14 : 0.0
                aiCandleColor = candleMove > 0.05 ? color.new(color.lime, 70) : candleMove < -0.05 ? color.new(color.red, 70) : color.new(color.orange, 70)
                candleX = bar_index + (k + 1) * visualStep
                array.push(fcDrawings, line.new(candleX, candleLow, candleX, candleHigh, xloc=xloc.bar_index, color=aiCandleColor, style=line.style_solid, width=1))
                array.push(fcDrawings, line.new(candleX, candleOpen, candleX, candleClose, xloc=xloc.bar_index, color=aiCandleColor, style=line.style_solid, width=4))
    if useaiForecast and not na(aiForecastForecastClose)
        aiPanelColor = aiForecastDirection == "UP" ? color.new(color.lime, 55) : aiForecastDirection == "DOWN" ? color.new(color.red, 55) : color.new(color.orange, 55)
        aiPanelMsg = "AI Forecast\n" + aiForecastDirection + " " + str.tostring(horizon) + "D\nTarget: " + str.tostring(aiForecastForecastClose, format.mintick) + "\n" + str.tostring(aiForecastPct, "#.##") + "% | Conf " + str.tostring(aiForecastConfidencePct, "#") + "%\nInvalid: " + str.tostring(aiForecastInvalidation, format.mintick) + "\nStatus: " + aiForecastStatus + "\nTol Acc: " + str.tostring(aiAccuracy20D, "#.##") + "%"
        array.push(fcDrawings, line.new(bar_index, aiForecastForecastClose, aiTargetEnd, aiForecastForecastClose, xloc=xloc.bar_index, color=color.new(color.black, 70), style=line.style_solid, width=1))
        // AI directional arrow: solid arrow line, width 2, trend color.
        array.push(fcDrawings, line.new(bar_index, close, commonForecastEnd, aiForecastForecastClose, xloc=xloc.bar_index, color=aiPanelColor, style=line.style_arrow_right, width=2))
        array.push(fcNotes, label.new(aiTargetEnd, aiForecastForecastClose, aiPanelMsg, xloc=xloc.bar_index, style=label.style_label_upper_left, color=aiPanelColor, textcolor=color.new(color.black, 10), size=size.tiny))

    // Short-term level lines (Support/Resistance/TR1/TR2/Stop/Entry), width 1, ending
    // 1 bar past the AI Forecast candlesticks (commonForecastEnd; shortened from
    // 2 bars in ML1.0), transparent, with a small bold-price tag at the right end.
    if showShortTermLevels
        srLineEnd = commonForecastEnd + 1
        f_levelLine(srLineEnd, shortSupport, "SUPPORT", color.orange, false)
        f_levelLine(srLineEnd, shortResistance, "RESISTANCE", color.lime, true)
        f_levelLine(srLineEnd, tr1Target, "TR1", color.green, false)
        f_levelLine(srLineEnd, tr2Target, "TR2", color.blue, false)
        f_levelLine(srLineEnd, shortStopLoss, "STOP LOSS", color.red, false)
        f_levelLine(srLineEnd, entryArea, "ENTRY-AREA", color.aqua, true)

    // ML1.0: execution-style recommendation at the last candle (see the
    // gate* variables defined near the decision engine above). Bull/bear
    // colored, transparent background, small bold text — same visual
    // language as the ENTRY-BUY/EXIT-SELL labels.
    gateLabelY = gateSide == "SELL" ? high + atr14 * 0.6 : low - atr14 * 0.6
    array.push(fcNotes, label.new(bar_index, gateLabelY, gateText, xloc=xloc.bar_index, style = gateSide == "SELL" ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, color = color.new(gateColor, notationTransparency), textcolor = color.new(color.black, 10), size = size.tiny))
    // UI FIX (2026-09-08): a separate "DECISION GATE 2.0" banner label used to
    // be drawn right here (3 lines, size.small, only ~1.0 ATR below/above the
    // legacy 1-line gate label above) — reported as visually colliding with
    // it and with the candle notation tags at this same price/bar location.
    // Its content is not lost: it's now the FIRST line of the floating panel
    // below (panelMsg), which is a single already-established UI surface
    // instead of a second competing label object.

// ---------- Elite 20D: plots — all lines made transparent per input (default 85%)
plot(showMA ? ema10 : na, "EMA10", color=color.new(color.aqua, lineTransparency), linewidth=1)
plot(showMA ? ema20 : na, "EMA20", color=color.new(color.blue, lineTransparency), linewidth=2)
plot(showMA ? ema50 : na, "EMA50", color=color.new(color.orange, lineTransparency), linewidth=2)
plot(showMA ? sma200 : na, "SMA200", color=color.new(color.purple, lineTransparency), linewidth=2)
plot(showLevels ? s1 : na, "Support 1", color=color.new(color.green, lineTransparency), linewidth=2, style=plot.style_stepline)
plot(showLevels ? s2 : na, "Support 2", color=color.new(color.green, lineTransparency), linewidth=1, style=plot.style_stepline)
plot(showLevels ? r1 : na, "Resistance 1", color=color.new(color.red, lineTransparency), linewidth=2, style=plot.style_stepline)
plot(showLevels ? r2 : na, "Resistance 2", color=color.new(color.red, lineTransparency), linewidth=1, style=plot.style_stepline)
pZL = plot(showBuyZone ? buyZoneLow : na, "Buy Zone Low", color=color.new(color.teal, 100))
pZH = plot(showBuyZone ? buyZoneHigh : na, "Buy Zone High", color=color.new(color.teal, 100))
fill(pZL, pZH, color=color.new(color.teal, 100), title="Buy Zone")
plot(hasPosition ? initialStop : buySignal ? autoStop : na, "Cut Loss", color=color.new(color.red, lineTransparency), linewidth=2, style=plot.style_stepline)
plot(hasPosition ? ownedTP1 : buySignal ? candidateTP1 : na, "Target 1", color=color.new(color.lime, lineTransparency), style=plot.style_stepline)
plot(hasPosition ? ownedTP2 : buySignal ? candidateTP2 : na, "Target 2", color=color.new(color.lime, lineTransparency), style=plot.style_stepline)
plot(hasPosition ? trailStop : na, "Trailing Stop", color=color.new(color.orange, lineTransparency), linewidth=2, style=plot.style_stepline)

// Forecast module analysis-only plots (Data Window / cross-tool reference).
// Forecast's own EMA20/EMA50 plots were dropped here — Elite's EMA20/EMA50
// plots above already cover the same series.
plot(invalidation, "Trend Forecast Invalidation (analysis only)", color=color.new(color.red, 100), style=plot.style_stepline, display=display.none)
plot(aiForecastForecastClose, "AI Forecast Target (analysis only)", display=display.none)
plot(aiForecastForecastClose + aiForecastBandAtr * atr14, "AI Forecast Upper Band (analysis only)", display=display.none)
plot(aiForecastForecastClose - aiForecastBandAtr * atr14, "AI Forecast Lower Band (analysis only)", display=display.none)

// ---------- Candle notations consolidated into 2 labels/bar (was 17 separate
// plotshape() calls — see V2.2 header note). One priority order picks at most
// one bullish (below-bar) and one bearish (above-bar) tag per bar.
isStd = displayMode == "Standard" or displayMode == "Detail"
isDetail = displayMode == "Detail"

bullTagText = bosBull ? "BOS+" : bearTrap ? "BRTRAP" : accClass == 3 ? "AK3" : (isStd and absorptionBull) ? "ABS+" : (isStd and accClass == 2) ? "AK2" : (isDetail and accClass == 1) ? "AK1" : ""
bullTagCol  = bosBull ? color.blue : bearTrap ? color.orange : absorptionBull and bullTagText == "ABS+" ? color.teal : color.green
bullTagDark = bullTagText == "AK1"

bearTagText = bosBear ? "BOS-" : (isStd and exhaustion) ? "EXH" : bullTrap ? "BTRAP" : upthrust ? "UT" : gapTrap ? "GTRAP" : distClass == 3 ? "DS3" : (isStd and absorptionBear) ? "ABS-" : (isStd and distClass == 2) ? "DS2" : (isDetail and churn) ? "CHURN" : (isDetail and distClass == 1) ? "DS1" : ""
bearTagCol  = bosBear ? color.red : exhaustion ? color.purple : (bullTrap or upthrust or gapTrap) ? color.orange : churn ? color.purple : absorptionBear and bearTagText == "ABS-" ? color.maroon : color.red
bearTagDark = bearTagText == "DS1"

var label[] noteLabels = array.new<label>()
f_capNotes() =>
    if array.size(noteLabels) > 100
        label.delete(array.shift(noteLabels))

if barstate.isconfirmed and bullTagText != ""
    nlB = label.new(bar_index, low - atr14 * 0.3, bullTagText, style = label.style_label_up, color = color.new(bullTagCol, notationTransparency), textcolor = color.new(color.black, 10), size = size.tiny)
    array.push(noteLabels, nlB)
    f_capNotes()
if barstate.isconfirmed and bearTagText != ""
    nlS = label.new(bar_index, high + atr14 * 0.3, bearTagText, style = label.style_label_down, color = color.new(bearTagCol, notationTransparency), textcolor = color.new(color.black, 10), size = size.tiny)
    array.push(noteLabels, nlS)
    f_capNotes()

// Decision label only when state changes; bounded queue avoids unlimited objects.
var label[] decisionLabels = array.new<label>()
decisionChanged = barstate.isconfirmed and decision != decision[1]
if showDecisionLabels and decisionChanged
    bool bullishDecision = str.contains(decision, "BUY") or decision == "PRE-BUY" or decision == "HOLD"
    bool bearishDecision = decision == "CL" or str.contains(decision, "X") or str.contains(decision, "SELL") or str.contains(decision, "RED")
    float y = bullishDecision ? low : high
    st = bullishDecision ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down
    color bg = bullishDecision ? color.new(color.green, notationTransparency) : bearishDecision ? color.new(color.red, notationTransparency) : color.new(color.gray, notationTransparency)
    label lb = label.new(bar_index, y, decision, style=st, color=bg, textcolor=color.new(color.black, 10), size=size.tiny)
    array.push(decisionLabels, lb)
    if array.size(decisionLabels) > maxDecisionLabels
        label.delete(array.shift(decisionLabels))

// ---------- ML1.2: floating, clearly-transparent info panel — only fields
// not already visible elsewhere on the chart (level lines, candle notation
// tags, TR/AI Forecast panel text) are kept, plus TR/AI Forecast summaries
// and a bottom BUY/SELL line. Anchored at the LAST bar with
// label.style_label_right, which grows the text LEFTWARD over
// already-rendered history — verified live in TradingView Desktop that this
// stays fully on-screen and unclipped regardless of window/panel layout,
// unlike ML1.1's bar_index+horizon/2 anchor with label.style_label_left
// (which — despite the name — grows text RIGHTWARD into however much empty
// future space happens to be visible, and clipped when that space shrank).
highest30 = ta.highest(high, 30)
// ML1.3: dashboardMode ("17. PRO — Dashboard/UI") picks Panel / Tabel Detail /
// both; showDashboard remains the master on/off switch for either.
showPanelNow = showDashboard and (dashboardMode == "Panel" or dashboardMode == "Panel + Tabel")
showTableNow = showDashboard and (dashboardMode == "Tabel Detail" or dashboardMode == "Panel + Tabel")
if barstate.islast and showPanelNow
    panelAnchorHigh = math.max(highest30, math.max(nz(aiForecastForecastClose, close), nz(trendForecastClose20, close)))
    panelY = panelAnchorHigh + 4 * atr14
    panelX = bar_index
    totalPatHits = array.get(hits, 0) + array.get(hits, 1) + array.get(hits, 2) + array.get(hits, 3)
    totalPatRes  = array.get(res, 0) + array.get(res, 1) + array.get(res, 2) + array.get(res, 3)
    patAccTxt = totalPatRes >= minStat ? str.tostring(math.round(100.0 * totalPatHits / totalPatRes)) + "% (" + str.tostring(totalPatHits) + "/" + str.tostring(totalPatRes) + ")" : "-"
    patLine = showStats ? "\nPattern Acc :    " + patAccTxt : ""
    // Fixed, clearly-transparent background (82) — verified live side-by-side
    // against ML1.1's notationTransparency-based fill (55), which read far
    // more opaque once actually rendered on chart.
    panelBg = str.contains(decision, "BUY") or decision == "HOLD" ? color.new(color.green, 82) : decision == "CL" or str.contains(decision, "X") or str.contains(decision, "RED") ? color.new(color.red, 82) : color.new(color.orange, 82)
    trFcTxt = direction + " " + str.tostring(forecastPct, "#.##") + "% (Conf " + str.tostring(confidence, "#") + "%)"
    aiFcTxt = not useaiForecast or na(aiForecastForecastClose) ? "OFF" : aiForecastDirection + " " + str.tostring(aiForecastPct, "#.##") + "% (Conf " + str.tostring(aiForecastConfidencePct, "#") + "%)"
    // BUG FIX (2026-09-08, v2.1): every value on this panel used to be wrapped
    // in f_bold(), which substitutes ASCII letters/digits for "Mathematical
    // Sans-Serif Bold" Unicode code points (U+1D5D4 range). Those code points
    // are outside the Basic Multilingual Plane and require a font that maps
    // them — on this user's actual TradingView Desktop they rendered as
    // garbled mojibake for EVERY value on the panel (confirmed by screenshot:
    // only the plain-ASCII labels like "SYMBOL :" stayed legible; every
    // f_bold()-wrapped value after each ":" was unreadable). Fixed by
    // dropping f_bold() everywhere in this file — plain text only. This is a
    // real readability regression fix, not a stylistic downgrade: unreadable
    // "bold" text conveys zero information, which is strictly worse than
    // plain text that conveys all of it.
    // STYLE (2026-09-08, v2.1): field labels changed from ALL-CAPS to
    // Capitalize-Each-Word per explicit request — recognized acronyms (ATR,
    // RVOL, TR, AI, MTF, RS) kept fully capitalized rather than mangled into
    // "Atr"/"Rvol"/etc., matching normal style-guide treatment of acronyms
    // inside title case. VALUES (decision codes, "BULL"/"BUY"/etc.) are left
    // untouched — several feed str.contains()/== checks elsewhere and must
    // keep their exact case.
    panelMsg = "Symbol :    " + syminfo.ticker + " . " + (hasPosition ? "OWNED" : "FLAT") +
               "\nDecision Gate 2.0 :    " + gate2Text + (conflictFlagPro ? " ⚠" : "") +
               "\nDecision :    " + decision +
               "\nTrend :    " + trendState + " (W:" + wState + ")" +
               "\nStructure :    " + structureText +
               "\nSetup :    " + setupCode +
               "\nCandle :    " + candleName +
               "\nRVOL/Flow :    " + str.tostring(rvol, "#.##") + "x / " + (flowRaw > 0 ? "BUY" : flowRaw < 0 ? "SELL" : "NEUTRAL") +
               "\nScore/Lot :    " + str.tostring(buyScore) + "/10 | " + str.tostring(lots) +
               "\nATR% :    " + str.tostring(atr14 / close * 100, "#.##") + "%" +
               "\nLevel Acc :    TR1 " + str.tostring(tr1Accuracy, "#.##") + "% . SR " + str.tostring(srConsistency, "#.##") + "%" +
               patLine +
               "\nTR Forecast :    " + trFcTxt +
               "\nAI Forecast :    " + aiFcTxt +
               "\nMTF/Market/RS :    " + mtfText + " . " + marketText + " . " + rsText +
               "\nS/R Pro :    " + str.tostring(support1, format.mintick) + " - " + str.tostring(resist1, format.mintick) +
               "\nBandarmologi :    " + bandarmologyText +
               "\nScore Pro :    " + str.tostring(bullScorePro, "#") + "/" + str.tostring(bearScorePro, "#") + " . " + gradePro +
               "\nAI Forecast 2.0 :    " + af2Direction + " (" + str.tostring(af2ConfidencePct, "#") + "%, edge kecil ~1pp tervalidasi)" +
               "\nGate 2.0 Plan :    " + gate2PlanStatusTxt +
               "\nBuy/Sell :    " + leadingGate + " -> " + gateText
    array.push(fcNotes, label.new(panelX, panelY, panelMsg, xloc=xloc.bar_index, style=label.style_label_right, color=panelBg, textcolor=color.new(color.black, 10), size=size.tiny))

// ---------- ML1.3: restored V2.4-style 6-column/21-row detail table, rebuilt
// against ML1.3's actual current variables (not a straight V2.4 copy — see
// header item 8): "Target Acc" fields renamed TOL ACC / JOINT ACC to match
// ML1.0's relabeling, and 4 new PRO rows (MTF/Market/Sector, S/R PRO,
// Bandarmologi, Bull/Bear Score+Grade) appended before the pattern hit-rate
// rows. Selectable via input `dashboardMode` ("17. PRO — Dashboard/UI").
var table dashPro = table.new(position.top_right, 6, 23, border_width=1)
f_cell6Pro(_row, _n1, _v1, _bg1, _n2, _v2, _bg2, _n3, _v3, _bg3) =>
    table.cell(dashPro, 0, _row, _n1, text_color=color.new(color.black, 10), bgcolor=color.new(color.silver, 30), text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(dashPro, 1, _row, _v1, text_color=color.new(color.black, 10), bgcolor=_bg1, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(dashPro, 2, _row, _n2, text_color=color.new(color.black, 10), bgcolor=color.new(color.silver, 30), text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(dashPro, 3, _row, _v2, text_color=color.new(color.black, 10), bgcolor=_bg2, text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(dashPro, 4, _row, _n3, text_color=color.new(color.black, 10), bgcolor=color.new(color.silver, 30), text_size=size.tiny)
    table.cell(dashPro, 5, _row, _v3, text_color=color.new(color.black, 10), bgcolor=_bg3, text_size=size.tiny)

if barstate.islast and showTableNow
    decisionColorT = str.contains(decision, "BUY") or decision == "HOLD" ? color.new(color.green, 10) : decision == "CL" or str.contains(decision, "X") or str.contains(decision, "RED") ? color.new(color.red, 5) : color.new(color.orange, 15)
    neutralBgT = color.new(color.gray, 30)
    fcDirColorT = direction == "UP" ? color.new(color.green, 10) : direction == "DOWN" ? color.new(color.red, 10) : neutralBgT
    fcConfColorT = confidence >= minConfidence ? color.new(color.green, 10) : neutralBgT
    fcStatusColorT = confidence >= minConfidence ? color.new(color.green, 10) : neutralBgT
    aiDirColorT = aiForecastDirection == "UP" ? color.new(color.green, 10) : aiForecastDirection == "DOWN" ? color.new(color.red, 10) : neutralBgT
    aiConfColorT = aiForecastConfidencePct >= minConfidence ? color.new(color.green, 10) : neutralBgT
    aiStatusColorT = aiForecastStatus == "VALID" ? color.new(color.green, 10) : neutralBgT
    f_cell6Pro(0, "IDXA-DG2.1", syminfo.ticker, color.new(color.blue, 20), "Position", hasPosition ? "OWNED" : "FLAT", hasPosition ? color.new(color.blue, 20) : neutralBgT, "TR Dir", direction, fcDirColorT)
    f_cell6Pro(1, "Weekly", wState, wBull ? color.new(color.green, 20) : wBear ? color.new(color.red, 10) : color.new(color.orange, 20), "Daily", trendState, dailyBullStrong ? color.new(color.green, 20) : dailyBear ? color.new(color.red, 10) : color.new(color.orange, 20), "TR Conf", str.tostring(confidence, "#") + "%", fcConfColorT)
    f_cell6Pro(2, "Structure", structureText, structureBull ? color.new(color.green, 30) : structureBear ? color.new(color.red, 20) : neutralBgT, "RVOL", str.tostring(rvol, "#.##") + "x / " + (flowRaw > 0 ? "BUY" : flowRaw < 0 ? "SELL" : "NEUTRAL"), volumeAnomaly ? color.new(color.purple, 10) : neutralBgT, "TR Fcst%", str.tostring(forecastPct, "#.##") + "%", neutralBgT)
    f_cell6Pro(3, "Accumulation", accClass == 3 ? "AK3" : accClass == 2 ? "AK2" : accClass == 1 ? "AK1" : "NONE", color.new(color.green, 35), "Distribution", distClass == 3 ? "DS3" : distClass == 2 ? "DS2" : distClass == 1 ? "DS1" : "NONE", color.new(color.red, 35), "TR Trend", dailyDrift > 0 ? "POSITIVE" : dailyDrift < 0 ? "NEGATIVE" : "FLAT", neutralBgT)
    f_cell6Pro(4, "Candle", candleName, candleBullScore >= 2 ? color.new(color.green, 25) : candleBearScore >= 2 ? color.new(color.red, 25) : neutralBgT, "Trap/Anomaly", trapText, trapText == "NONE" ? neutralBgT : color.new(color.orange, 10), "TR Status", confidence >= minConfidence ? "VALID" : "LOW CONF", fcStatusColorT)
    f_cell6Pro(5, "Setup", setupCode, color.new(color.blue, 30), "Score/Lot", str.tostring(buyScore) + "/10 | " + str.tostring(lots), color.new(color.gray, 25), "TR Invalid", str.tostring(invalidation, format.mintick), color.new(color.red, 20))
    f_cell6Pro(6, "Support", str.tostring(s1, format.mintick), color.new(color.green, 35), "Resistance", str.tostring(r1, format.mintick), color.new(color.red, 35), "TR Dir Acc", str.tostring(directionAccuracy20D, "#.##") + "%", directionAccuracy20D >= 60 ? color.new(color.green, 10) : neutralBgT)
    f_cell6Pro(7, "Entry / Avg", str.tostring(hasPosition ? entryPrice : candidateEntry, format.mintick), color.new(color.blue, 30), "Stop", str.tostring(hasPosition ? initialStop : autoStop, format.mintick), color.new(color.red, 20), "TR Tol Acc", str.tostring(accuracy20D, "#.##") + "%", accuracy20D >= 55 ? color.new(color.green, 10) : neutralBgT)
    f_cell6Pro(8, "Target 2", str.tostring(hasPosition ? ownedTP2 : candidateTP2, format.mintick), color.new(color.green, 25), "Decision", decision, decisionColorT, "Eval Timeline", str.tostring(horizon) + "D (SAMA)", neutralBgT)
    f_cell6Pro(9, "ATR%", str.tostring(atr14 / close * 100, "#.##") + "%", neutralBgT, "AI Dir", aiForecastDirection, aiDirColorT, "AI Target", str.tostring(aiForecastForecastClose, format.mintick), neutralBgT)
    f_cell6Pro(10, "AI Fcst%", str.tostring(aiForecastPct, "#.##") + "%", neutralBgT, "AI Conf", str.tostring(aiForecastConfidencePct, "#") + "%", aiConfColorT, "AI Invalid", str.tostring(aiForecastInvalidation, format.mintick), color.new(color.red, 20))
    f_cell6Pro(11, "AI Status", aiForecastStatus, aiStatusColorT, "AI Tol Acc", str.tostring(aiAccuracy20D, "#.##") + "%", aiAccuracy20D >= 55 ? color.new(color.green, 10) : neutralBgT, "AI Dir Acc", str.tostring(aiDirectionAccuracy20D, "#.##") + "%", aiDirectionAccuracy20D >= 60 ? color.new(color.green, 10) : neutralBgT)
    f_cell6Pro(12, "AI Blend", str.tostring(aiForecastActiveWeight * 100, "#") + "%", neutralBgT, "AI Dispersion", na(aiForecastDisp) ? "WAIT" : str.tostring(aiForecastDisp * 100, "#.##") + "%", na(aiForecastDisp) or aiForecastDisp < 0.03 ? color.new(color.green, 10) : neutralBgT, "TR1 Joint Acc", str.tostring(tr1Accuracy, "#.##") + "%", tr1Accuracy >= 55 ? color.new(color.green, 10) : neutralBgT)
    f_cell6Pro(13, "SR Consist", str.tostring(srConsistency, "#.##") + "%", srConsistency >= 60 ? color.new(color.green, 10) : neutralBgT, "Entry Area", str.tostring(entryArea, format.mintick), color.new(color.blue, 25), "SR Window", str.tostring(srLookback) + "D", neutralBgT)
    f_cell6Pro(14, "MTF (HTF)", mtfText, mtfBias == 1 ? color.new(color.green, 20) : mtfBias == -1 ? color.new(color.red, 10) : neutralBgT, "Market Idx", marketText, marketBias == 1 ? color.new(color.green, 20) : marketBias == -1 ? color.new(color.red, 10) : neutralBgT, "Sector RS", rsText, rsBias == 1 ? color.new(color.green, 20) : rsBias == -1 ? color.new(color.red, 10) : neutralBgT)
    f_cell6Pro(15, "S/R Pro Sup", str.tostring(support1, format.mintick), color.new(color.green, 35), "S/R Pro Res", str.tostring(resist1, format.mintick), color.new(color.red, 35), "Tightness", str.tostring(tfTightnessPro, "#.##"), neutralBgT)
    f_cell6Pro(16, "Bandarmologi", bandarmologyAnomalyTxt, isAnomalyTrapPro ? color.new(color.orange, 10) : neutralBgT, "Akum/Dist", bandarmologyVolTxt == "" ? "NETRAL" : bandarmologyVolTxt, gradualAccumPro ? color.new(color.green, 20) : gradualDistPro ? color.new(color.red, 10) : neutralBgT, "Flow Phase", phaseTextPro, phaseBiasPro == 1 ? color.new(color.green, 20) : phaseBiasPro == -1 ? color.new(color.red, 10) : neutralBgT)
    f_cell6Pro(17, "Bull Score", str.tostring(bullScorePro, "#"), color.new(color.green, 100 - int(bullScorePro * 0.6)), "Bear Score", str.tostring(bearScorePro, "#"), color.new(color.red, 100 - int(bearScorePro * 0.6)), "Grade", gradePro, str.contains(gradePro, "A") ? color.new(color.green, 10) : str.contains(gradePro, "D") ? color.new(color.red, 10) : color.new(color.orange, 15))
    f_cell6Pro(18, "Gate 2.0", gate2Dir, gate2Dir == "BUY BIAS" ? color.new(color.green, 15) : gate2Dir == "SELL/AVOID BIAS" ? color.new(color.red, 10) : neutralBgT, "Conviction", gate2Tier, neutralBgT, "Lot Sugesti", str.tostring(lotsConvictionPro) + "/" + str.tostring(lots), conflictFlagPro ? color.new(color.orange, 10) : neutralBgT)
    f_cell6Pro(19, "AI Forecast 2.0", af2Direction + " " + str.tostring(af2ConfidencePct, "#") + "%", af2Direction == "UP" ? color.new(color.green, 25) : color.new(color.red, 25), "Gate 2.0 Plan", gate2InPlan ? "AKTIF" : "-", gate2InPlan ? color.new(color.blue, 20) : neutralBgT, "Trail Stop", gate2InPlan ? str.tostring(gate2PlanStop, format.mintick) : "-", neutralBgT)
    if showStats
        table.cell(dashPro, 0, 20, "Pattern", text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.tiny, bgcolor=color.new(color.gray, 90))
        table.cell(dashPro, 1, 20, "Reached Target", text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.tiny, bgcolor=color.new(color.gray, 90))
        table.cell(dashPro, 2, 20, "Pattern", text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.tiny, bgcolor=color.new(color.gray, 90))
        table.cell(dashPro, 3, 20, "Reached Target", text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.tiny, bgcolor=color.new(color.gray, 90))
        table.cell(dashPro, 4, 20, "Pattern", text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.tiny, bgcolor=color.new(color.gray, 90))
        table.cell(dashPro, 5, 20, "Reached Target", text_color=color.gray, text_size=size.tiny, bgcolor=color.new(color.gray, 90))
        dtRt = array.get(res, 0)
        dtHt = array.get(hits, 0)
        dbRt = array.get(res, 1)
        dbHt = array.get(hits, 1)
        hsRt = array.get(res, 2)
        hsHt = array.get(hits, 2)
        ihRt = array.get(res, 3)
        ihHt = array.get(hits, 3)
        dtTxtT = showDT and dtRt >= minStat ? str.tostring(dtHt) + "/" + str.tostring(dtRt) + " " + str.tostring(math.round(100.0 * dtHt / dtRt)) + "%" : "-"
        dbTxtT = showDB and dbRt >= minStat ? str.tostring(dbHt) + "/" + str.tostring(dbRt) + " " + str.tostring(math.round(100.0 * dbHt / dbRt)) + "%" : "-"
        hsTxtT = showHS and hsRt >= minStat ? str.tostring(hsHt) + "/" + str.tostring(hsRt) + " " + str.tostring(math.round(100.0 * hsHt / hsRt)) + "%" : "-"
        ihTxtT = showIHS and ihRt >= minStat ? str.tostring(ihHt) + "/" + str.tostring(ihRt) + " " + str.tostring(math.round(100.0 * ihHt / ihRt)) + "%" : "-"
        f_cell6Pro(21, "Double Top", dtTxtT, bearCol, "Double Bottom", dbTxtT, bullCol, "Head & Shoulders", hsTxtT, bearCol)
        f_cell6Pro(22, "Inverse H&S", ihTxtT, bullCol, "", "", neutralBgT, "", "", neutralBgT)

// ---------- Alerts: Elite 20D
alertcondition(buySignal, "BUY Setup Confirmed", "{{ticker}} BUY setup confirmed on {{interval}}. Check entry, stop, target and dashboard.")
alertcondition(buySignalReversal, "BUY Reversal (RV2)", "{{ticker}} reversal BUY via support + candlestick + volume confluence, ahead of the weekly trend gate.")
alertcondition(preBuy, "PRE-BUY", "{{ticker}} PRE-BUY: accumulation and structure detected; wait for trigger.")
alertcondition(bullTrap or upthrust or gapTrap, "Trading Trap", "{{ticker}} trading trap detected: avoid new buy or manage owned position.")
alertcondition(distClass >= 2, "Distribution", "{{ticker}} medium/large distribution proxy detected.")
alertcondition(hasPosition and tp1Hit, "Target 1", "{{ticker}} Target 1 reached: consider partial take profit.")
alertcondition(hasPosition and tp2Hit, "Target 2", "{{ticker}} Target 2 reached: manage remaining position.")
alertcondition(hasPosition and (hardStopHit or structureExit or falseBreakExit), "SELL / Cut Loss", "{{ticker}} SELL/CUT-LOSS condition detected. Review final decision.")
alertcondition(hasPosition and timeExit, "20-Day Time Exit", "{{ticker}} 20-day time exit condition detected.")

// ---------- Alerts: Chart Patterns
alertcondition(bearConf, "[Pattern] Bearish pattern confirmed", "A bearish reversal pattern broke its neckline")
alertcondition(bullConf, "[Pattern] Bullish pattern confirmed", "A bullish reversal pattern broke its neckline")
alertcondition(tgtHit, "[Pattern] Target reached", "A confirmed pattern reached its measured target")
alertcondition(patFail, "[Pattern] Pattern invalidated", "A confirmed pattern was invalidated before reaching target")

// ---------- Alerts: Forecast
alertcondition(barstate.isconfirmed and direction == "UP" and confidence >= minConfidence, "20D Trend Forecast UP", "{{ticker}} forecast 20D UP with valid confidence. Review risk and invalidation.")
alertcondition(barstate.isconfirmed and direction == "DOWN" and confidence >= minConfidence, "20D Trend Forecast DOWN", "{{ticker}} forecast 20D DOWN. Review owned position and invalidation.")
alertcondition(validationTrue, "Forecast Validation Passed", "{{ticker}} locked rolling forecast validation passed.")
alertcondition(validationFalse, "Forecast Validation Failed", "{{ticker}} locked rolling forecast validation failed; recalibrate or reduce reliance.")
